iU="TOPIC",sU="Data storage: Sound",nU=null,oU=null,cU=25,lU=[{question_id:"1",parent_question:1,topic:"digital sound storage terms",marks:6,command_word:"complete",content:[{type:"text",value:"A student is creating a presentation containing images and sound."},{type:"text",value:"One of the files is an audio recording."},{type:"text",value:"Complete the description of how a computer stores sound. Fill in the gaps using the given list of terms. Not all terms will be used."},{type:"text",value:"Terms: analogue, colour depth, higher, repeated, smaller, binary, digital, lower, sample rate, unique, bit depth, height, measuring, sampling, byte, hertz, recording, seconds"},{type:"text",value:"An ____ sound wave needs to be converted into a digital sound wave."},{type:"text",value:"Sound ____ is when the amplitude of the sound wave is measured at set intervals."},{type:"text",value:"The ____ is the number of times a second the sound wave is measured. This is given in Hertz."},{type:"text",value:"Each amplitude is given a ____ binary number. The number of bits allocated to each sample is the ____."},{type:"text",value:"The ____ the number of bits, the wider the number of amplitudes can be measured."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for each completed gap: analogue, sampling, sample rate, unique, bit depth, higher.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"analogue",marks:1},{criteria:"sampling",marks:1},{criteria:"sample rate",marks:1},{criteria:"unique",marks:1},{criteria:"bit depth",marks:1},{criteria:"higher",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(i)",parent_question:2,topic:"sound sampling definition",marks:1,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"A musician uses a computer to make and record music."},{type:"text",value:"Tick one box to identify the correct description of sound sampling."},{type:"table",headers:["","The frequency of the wave is measured a set number of times each second.","The amplitude of the wave is measured at set intervals.","The digital sound wave is measured a se