:1}]}}],fT={paper_id:aU,qualification:rU,component:iU,title:sU,year:nU,session:oU,total_marks:cU,questions:lU},dU="J277-TOPIC-1.2.9",pU="J277",uU="TOPIC",mU="Compression",hU=null,gU=null,fU=17,yU=[{question_id:"1(i)",parent_question:1,topic:"text compression method",marks:3,command_word:"identify and justify",content:[{type:"text",value:"A student has a text document and an image file that need to be compressed separately."},{type:"text",value:"The student needs to reduce the file size of both of these files as much as possible."},{type:"text",value:"Identify the most suitable type of compression for the text document. Justify your choice."},{type:"text",value:"Type of compression: ____"},{type:"text",value:"Justification: ____"}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for lossless. Up to 2 marks for justification. Valid points include that lossless removes no data, the file can be reconstructed exactly, and text files need all data to remain accurate and usable.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct type identified: lossless",marks:1},{criteria:"A valid justification about preserving all data",marks:1},{criteria:"A valid justification linked to text files remaining accurate and usable",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"1(ii)",parent_question:1,topic:"image compression method",marks:3,command_word:"identify and justify",content:[{type:"text",value:"Identify the most suitable type of compression for the image file. Justify your choice."},{type:"text",value:"Type of compression: ____"},{type:"text",value:"Justification: ____"}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark for lossy. Up to 2 marks for justification. Valid points include that lossy reduces file size more than lossless and that small losses in image quality may not be noticed by the user.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Correct type identified: lossy",marks:1},{criteria:"A valid justification about a larger reduction in file size",marks:1},{criteria:"A valid justification about image quality loss being less noticeable",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(i)",parent_question:2,topic:"compression benefits",marks:2,command_word:"give",content:[{type:"text",value:"A student compresses all their documents before emailing them to their teacher."},{type:"text",value:"Give two benefits of compressing the data before it is emailed."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each to a maximum of 2. Valid benefits include reduced file size, faster transmission or upload/download, less storage space required, less bandwidth used, or less data sent.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"One valid benefit of compression is given",marks:1},{criteria:"A second valid benefit of compression is given",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2(ii)",parent_question:2,topic:"lossy compression drawbacks",marks:2,command_word:"explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"Explain why lossy compression may not be appropriate to compress all of the student's files."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark each to a maximum of 2. Valid points include that data is permanently lost or not fully recoverable, text files cannot be compressed with lossy compression, or the teacher may need the original or high-quality image, video, or sound files.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Lossy compression permanently removes data or cannot fully recover the original",marks:1},{criteria:"Text files cannot use lossy compression, or original quality may be required",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"3(i)",parent_question:3,topic:"why compress media before upload",marks:2,command_word:"explain",content:[{type:"text",value:"Layla is an artist. She draws images by hand. The image is then scanned and stored on a computer."},{type:"text",value:"Layla uploads her images and videos to a website."},{type:"text",value:"Explain why Layla compresses the images and videos before uploading them."}],answer:{guidance:"1 mark per point to a maximum of 2. Compression reduces the file size, so the files take less space on the server and upload or download faster.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"The file size is reduced or less server space is needed",