e expensive for large amounts of data / long term / hosting // may be ongoing subscription // no control over changing costs May be limited amount of storage No control over security // Need to rely on provider for security May be hacked/stolen/intercepted/affected by a virus May lose (personal) data // May lose access to data May go against DPA/legislation // Data may be misused (by provider) May not be clear where in the world the data is stored Limited/No control over access Company/cloud could go down No control over backup // May not have (automatic) backups … … data is not retrievable Need internet access // no internet access means no data … access speed depends on network/connection speed Concerns over ownership of the data Need to remember login details // may forget/lose login details Users may need training MP1 needs more than high cost, it needs identification of ongoing, cost for hosting etc. MP3 just poor/low security is NE Accept: data may be sold as example of misuse.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for one valid cloud-storage drawback from: ongoing/expensive for large amounts/long-term/hosting (cost identification beyond just 'high cost'); limited amount of storage; no control over security / reliance on provider for security ('poor/low security' alone is NE); may be hacked/stolen/intercepted/affected by virus; may lose (personal) data or access to it; may go against DPA/legislation, data may be misused (accept: data may be sold); may not be clear where data is stored geographically; limited/no control over access; company/cloud could go down; no control over backup, may not have automatic backups, data not retrievable; requires internet access (access speed depends on connection); concerns over data ownership; need to remember login details; users may need training.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for a second distinct drawback from the same list.","marks":1},{"criteria":"Award 1 mark for a third distinct drawback from the same 