ion was completed very well by the vast majority of candidates, showing that data types are now well understood.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"teamName: String","marks":1},{"criteria":"studentYearGroup: Integer","marks":1},{"criteria":"javelinThrow: Real / Float","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(a)(ii)","parent_question":5,"topic":"linear-search-function","marks":4,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The student names for a team are stored in an array with the identifier `theTeam`. An example of the data in this array is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","0","1","2","3","4","5"],"rows":[["Data","Ali","Eve","Ling","Nina","Sarah","Tom"]]},{"type":"text","value":"A linear search function is used to find whether a student is in the team. The function:\\n- takes a student name as a parameter\\n- returns True if the student name is in the array\\n- returns False if the student name is not in the array.\\n\\nComplete the design of an algorithm for the linear search function."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"function linearSearch(studentName)\\n  for count = 0 to ____\\n    if theTeam[____] == ____ then\\n      return ____\\n    endif\\n  next count\\n  return False\\nendfunction"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept 6 // theTeam.length() for BP1 (Python). Accept alternative length functions e.g. len(). Accept count = 5 (and equivalents) for BP1.\\n\\nAccept \\"True\\" for BP4. Do not allow obvious spaces in variable names. Ignore capitalisation.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"theTeam.length() - 1 // 5","marks":1},{"criteria":"count (as index)","marks":1},{"criteria":"studentName","marks":1},{"criteria":"True","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(b)","parent_question":5,"topic":"trace-table-javelin-score","marks":4,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"This algorithm calculates the number of points a student gets for the distance they throw in the javelin:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"01 javelinThrow