arch results, rating, message)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8","parent_question":8,"topic":"refine-search-count","marks":4,"command_word":"Refine","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An array stores a collection of words. The array has the identifier `data`."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"data = [\\"or\\", \\"and\\", \\"it\\", \\"when\\", \\"and\\", \\"or\\", \\"and\\", \\"it\\"]"},{"type":"text","value":"A searching algorithm is used to find a word in the array `data`. The algorithm used to search for a word is shown."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"word = input(\\"Enter a word to find\\")\\nfound = False\\nfor i = 0 to 7\\n  if data[i] == word then\\n    found = True\\n  endif\\nnext i\\nprint(found)"},{"type":"text","value":"Some words appear in the array more than once.\\n\\nRefine the algorithm to:\\n- count the number of times a word appears in the array\\n- output this number.\\n\\nFor example, the algorithm should output 3 if the input is \\"and\\"."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example answer:\\n\\n```\\nsearch = input(\\"Enter a word\\")\\ncount = 0\\nfor i = 0 to 7\\n  if data[i] == search then\\n    count = count + 1\\nnext i\\nprint(count)\\n```\\n\\nAllow answers that completely rewrite the algorithm as long as points on left met.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Declares variable to store the count (before the for loop)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Initialises variable to zero","marks":1},{"criteria":"Increments variable by 1 each time the word is found","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs count value","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9(a)(i)","parent_question":9,"topic":"sql-select-where-and","marks":4,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Drones flies goods around the country using drones.\\n\\nDetails about the drones that pilots fly are stored in a database table called TblDrone. Some of the data stored in this table is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["DroneID","DroneType","Mileage","LastCheck"],"rows":[["001