ent)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(b)(i)","parent_question":10,"topic":"arithmetic-operator-power","marks":1,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Three incomplete pseudocode algorithms are given with a description of the purpose of each algorithm.\\n\\nWrite the missing arithmetic operator for each algorithm.\\n\\nOutputting 12 to the power of 2."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"print(12 ____ 2)"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept ** or other sensible operator that indicates raising to a power. If pseudocode operator given, must be a single word/symbol (e.g. pow), not containing spaces.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"^ (or ** / pow etc)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(b)(ii)","parent_question":10,"topic":"arithmetic-operator","marks":1,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Working out if a number is odd or even."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"number = 53\\nif number ____ 2 == 0 then\\n  print(\\"Even number\\")\\nelse\\n  print(\\"Odd number\\")\\nendif"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept % or other sensible operator that indicates modulus. If pseudocode operator given, must be a single word/symbol (e.g. modulo), not containing spaces.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"MOD (or % / modulo)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(b)(iii)","parent_question":10,"topic":"arithmetic-operator-subtraction","marks":1,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Finding the difference between two measurements."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"measurement1 = 300\\nmeasurement2 = 100\\ndifference = measurement1 ____ measurement2"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept other sensible operator that indicates subtraction. If a pseudocode operator given, must be a single word/symbol (e.g. minus), not containing spaces.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"- (minus)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(c)","parent_question":10,"topic":"trace-table-do-until","marks":3,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the following pseudocode algorithm:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"01 start = 3\\n02 do\\n03 print(start)\\n04 start = start - 1\\n05 until start == -1\\n06 print(\\"Finished\\")"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following trace table for the given algorithm."},{"type":"table","headers":["Line number","start","Output"],"rows":[["","",""],["","",""],["","",""],["","",""],["","",""],["","",""],["","",""],["","",""],["","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Ignore lines 02 and 05 in answer unless these change or output any values. Candidate may repeat start value when unchanged, this is acceptable.\\n\\nPenalise incorrect or missing line numbers or additional output once only then FT. -1 must not be output for BP2. Penalise missing or incorrect output once only for BP1 and FT for missing or incorrect output for BP2.\\n\\nFinished may be with or without quotes. Ignore case or minor spelling error. Max 2 marks if any incorrect output or changes to start. Do not accept calculated values of start (e.g. 3-1).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Start is set to 3 on line 01 and 3 is output on line 03","marks":1},{"criteria":"2, 1 and 0 are output on next 3 iterations with start updated to 2, 1, 0, -1 on correct line numbers","marks":1},{"criteria":"Finished is output on line 06","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"11","parent_question":11,"topic":"increment-variable","marks":1,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write pseudocode to increment a value held in a variable score by one."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Allow other logically correct answers that result in score increasing by one and being overwritten. Do not accept score + 1 / score = +1.\\n\\nAccept valid structured English answers that refer to score increasing and overwriting the existing value by one. e.g. \\"score becomes/equals score plus one\\". Ignore any superfluous code that does not affect the outcome.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"score = score + 1 // score += 1 // score++","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12","parent_question":12,"topic":"total-and-average-algorithm","marks":6,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Jack is writing a program to add up some numbers. His first attempt at the program is shown."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"a = input(\\"Enter a number\\")\\nb = input(\\"Enter a number\\")\\nc = input(\\"Enter a number\\")\\nd = input(\\"Enter a number\\")\\ne = input(\\"Enter a number\\")\\nf = (a + b + c + d + e)\\nprint(f)"},{"type":"text","value":"Jack decides to improve his program. He wants to be able to input how many numbers to add together each time the algorithm runs, and also wants it to calculate and display the average of these numbers.\\n\\nWrite an algorithm to:\\n- ask the user to input the quantity of numbers they want to enter and read this value as input\\n- repeatedly take a number as input, until the quantity of numbers the user input has been entered\\n- calculate and output the total of these numbers\\n- calculate and output the average of these numbers."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\n\\n```\\nnum = input(\\"Enter how many numbers\\")\\nfor x = 1 to num\\n  temp = input(\\"Enter a number\\")\\n  total = total + temp\\nnext x\\nprint(total)\\nprint(total / num)\\n```\\n\\nIf flow chart used, correct shapes needed. Allow tolerance of 1 with number of loops for BP3 with for loops. BP1 requires input with a message (can be two statements, e.g. print and then input or combined). Input must be stored or used.\\n\\nBP3, 4, 5 must be logically correct to be credited. Ignore non-initialisation of total. BP5 can be given as FT as long as an attempt has been made at working out a total within the loop. BP6 can be given as FT long as attempt made at total and average (not necessarily in a loop).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"input and stores/uses value with message","marks":1},{"criteria":"attempt at repeating","marks":1},{"criteria":"correctly repeats number of times given as input","marks":1},{"criteria":"correctly take number as input within loop and calculates total of these numbers","marks":1},{"criteria":"correctly calculate an average (total/num)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Output both total and average","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"13(a)(i)","parent_question":13,"topic":"hotel-booking-validation","marks":5,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Customers at a hotel can stay between 1 and 5 (inclusive) nights and can choose between a basic room or a premium room.\\n\\nWhen a new booking is recorded, the details are entered into a program to validate the values. The following criteria are checked:\\n- firstName and surname are not empty\\n- room is either \\"basic\\" or \\"premium\\"\\n- nights is between 1 and 5 (inclusive).\\n\\nIf any invalid data is found \\"NOT ALLOWED\\" is displayed.\\nIf all data is valid \\"ALLOWED\\" is displayed.\\n\\nComplete the following program to validate the inputs.\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n- OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n- a high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"firstName = input(\\"Enter a first name\\")\\nsurname = input(\\"Enter a surname\\")\\nroom = input(\\"Enter basic or premium\\")\\nnights = input(\\"Enter between 1 and 5 nights\\")\\nstayComplete = False"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\n\\n```\\nvalid = True\\nif firstname == \\"\\" or surname == \\"\\" then\\n  valid = False\\nend if\\nif room != \\"basic\\" and room != \\"premium\\" then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif nights < 1 or nights > 5 then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif valid then\\n  print(\\"ALLOWED\\")\\nelse\\n  print(\\"NOT ALLOWED\\")\\nendif\\n```\\n\\nMust have some attempt at all three checks to give output mark(s). Check for nights must check both upper and lower limits. Iteration can be used as validation if input repeatedly asked for until valid answer given.\\n\\nDo not accept logically incorrect Boolean conditions such as \'if firstname or surname == \\"\\"\'. BP1 to 3 can check for valid or invalid inputs. Pay particular attention to use of AND / OR. Only give marks for output if these work together correctly.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Checks that both firstname and surname are not empty","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks that room is either \\"basic\\" or \\"premium\\"","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks that nights is between 1 and 5 (inclusive)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"NOT ALLOWED\\" (or equivalent) if any of the 3 checks are invalid","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"ALLOWED\\" (or equivalent) only if all three checks are valid","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"13(a)(ii)","parent_question":13,"topic":"test-plan-nights","marks":3,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following test plan to check whether the number of nights is validated correctly."},{"type":"table","headers":["Test data (number of nights)","Type of test","Expected output"],"rows":[["2","","ALLOWED"],["","Boundary","ALLOWED"],["","Erroneous / Invalid","NOT ALLOWED"]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Allow other descriptions that mean normal (e.g. valid / typical / acceptable).\\n\\nTest data 2: Normal, ALLOWED.\\nTest data 1 // 5: Boundary, ALLOWED (not 0 or 6 as says allowed).\\nTest data e.g. 7: Erroneous/Invalid, NOT ALLOWED (any numeric value except 1 to 5 // any non-numeric input e.g. \\"bananas\\").","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Normal (type for test data 2)","marks":1},{"criteria":"1 or 5 (boundary test data, not 0 or 6)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Any numeric value except 1 to 5 // non-numeric (erroneous test data)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"13(b)(i)","parent_question":13,"topic":"newprice-function","marks":4,"command_word":"Create","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A Basic room costs £60 each night. A Premium room costs £80 each night.\\n\\nCreate a function, `newPrice()`, that takes the number of nights and the type of room as parameters, calculates and returns the price to pay.\\n\\nYou do not have to validate these parameters.\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n- OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n- a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\n\\n```\\nfunction newPrice(nights, room)\\n  if room == \\"basic\\" then\\n    price = 60 * nights\\n  elseif room == \\"premium\\" then\\n    price = 80 * nights\\n  endif\\n  return price\\nendfunction\\n```\\n\\nBP1 must be clear that a new function is being defined. E.g. function / def keyword. Allow FT for subsequent marks if not present. Ignore any code outside attempt at function definition. Ignore additional parameters. Ignore inputs or additional code as long as these do not overwrite parameters. If inputs used instead of parameters, FT for BP3.\\n\\nAllow use of else for second room type in BP3. Must return (not output) value. Return can be done e.g. in VB by assigning to function name (e.g. newPrice = price).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Function header for newPrice","marks":1},{"criteria":"...taking (at least) two parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"...correctly calculates price based on parameters within function","marks":1},{"criteria":"...returns this calculated price","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"13(b)(ii)","parent_question":13,"topic":"newprice-function-call","marks":3,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write program code, that uses `newPrice()`, to output the price of staying in a Premium room for 5 nights.\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n- OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n- a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\n\\n```\\nprint(newPrice(\\"premium\\", 5))\\n```\\n\\nor\\n\\n```\\nx = newPrice(5, \\"premium\\")\\nprint(x)\\n```\\n\\nOrder of parameters not important. \\"premium\\" must use string delimiters (e.g. quotes). Do not allow function definitions for BP1. Ignore capitalisation of newPrice.\\n\\nCandidate could store returned value in a variable and then print this, or store parameters in variables before passing in. Ignore any superfluous code given. Do not credit answers where newPrice is overwritten prior to use. Ignore spaces. Allow function call if brackets missing.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Call function newPrice","marks":1},{"criteria":"...with (\\"premium\\", 5) as parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"Output returned value","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"13(c)","parent_question":13,"topic":"refine-logic-errors","marks":2,"command_word":"Describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A hotel has nine rooms that are numbered from room 0 to room 8.\\n\\nThe number of people currently staying in each room is stored in an array with the identifier room.\\n\\nThe index of room represents the room number."},{"type":"text","value":"Array `room`"},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","0","1","2","3","4","5","6","7","8"],"rows":[["Data","2","1","3","2","1","0","0","4","1"]]},{"type":"text","value":"The following program counts how many people are currently staying in the hotel."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"for count = 1 to 8\\n  total = 0\\n  total = total + room[count]\\nnext count\\nprint(total)"},{"type":"text","value":"When tested, the program is found to contain two logic errors.\\n\\nDescribe how the program can be refined to remove these logic errors."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Allow loop changed to 0 to 8 or 0 to 9 (Python). Do not accept moving total outside loop if moved to after loop (would still be a logic error). Do not accept move to top of loop.\\n\\nAccept corrected code shown. Accept reference to count variable limits for BP1.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"For loop changed to include 0 (e.g. 0 to 8)","marks":1},{"criteria":"total = 0 moved to before loop starts / removed","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"13(d)","parent_question":13,"topic":"car-park-pricing-loop","marks":6,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A hotel car park charges £4 per hour. If the car is electric, this price is halved to £2 per hour.\\n\\nWrite an algorithm to:\\n- take as input the number of hours the user has parked and whether their car is electric or not\\n- calculate and output the total price\\n- repeat continually until the user enters 0 hours.\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n- OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n- a high level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\n\\n```\\nwhile hours != 0\\n  hours = input(\\"Enter hours\\")\\n  electric = input(\\"enter Y for electric or N\\")\\n  if electric == \\"Y\\" then\\n    price = hours * 2\\n  elseif electric == \\"N\\" then\\n    price = hours * 4\\n  endif\\n  print(price)\\nendwhile\\n```\\n\\nInitialisation of price and hours not necessary, but if present hours must be non-zero for BP6 to be given. BP5 must include all points attempted.\\n\\nBP6 can be given as FT even if BP5 (loop) is in the wrong place. BP6 could be achieved as repeated function calls / recursion.\\n\\nInitial input outside of loop that is then also included within loop is fine. Do not accept while hours > 0 (could be -1). Do not penalise answers where 0 is output when loop exits.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Inputs hours AND electric (two separate inputs), storing or using these","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks if car is electric (IF/Select statement)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...correctly calculates and outputs price (hours * 2 // price / 2) for electric","marks":1},{"criteria":"...correctly calculates and outputs price (hours * 4 // electric price * 2) for non-electric","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at repetition of above","marks":1},{"criteria":"...until 0 hours entered","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"14(a)","parent_question":14,"topic":"truth-table-nand","marks":2,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete the truth table in Fig. 1 for the Boolean statement P = NOT(A AND B)."},{"type":"table","headers":["A","B","P"],"rows":[["0","0","1"],["0","1","____"],["1","0","____"],["1","1","0"]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for each correct answer in table. \'True\' or \'T\' are also credit worthy.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"P = 1 for A=0, B=1","marks":1},{"criteria":"P = 1 for A=1, B=0","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"14(b)","parent_question":14,"topic":"logic-diagram-nand","marks":1,"command_word":"Tick","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Tick (✓) one box to identify the correct logic diagram for P = NOT(A AND B).\\n\\nP = NOT(A AND B)"},{"type":"table","headers":["Logic diagram","Tick one box"],"rows":[[{"type":"image","kind":"diagram","src":"j277/yearpapers/specimen/1b/a.png","alt_text":"Option a logic-gate diagram."},""],[{"type":"image","kind":"diagram","src":"j277/yearpapers/specimen/1b/b.png","alt_text":"Option b logic-gate diagram."},""],[{"type":"image","kind":"diagram","src":"j277/yearpapers/specimen/1b/c.png","alt_text":"Option c logic-gate diagram."},""]]}],"answer":{"auto_mark":{"type":"single_tick_table","correct_key":"1:1"},"guidance":"Correct Answer Only. The correct logic diagram is the NAND gate equivalent (AND followed by NOT).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Correct logic diagram identified (NAND / AND-NOT)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"15(a)","parent_question":15,"topic":"pseudocode-max-of-two","marks":4,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A program needs to perform the following tasks:\\n- Input two numbers from the user\\n- Compare both numbers and output the largest number.\\n\\nComplete the pseudocode for this program."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"num1 = input(\\"enter first number\\")\\nnum2 = input(\\"enter second number\\")\\n____ num1 > ____ then\\n  ____\\nelse\\n  ____\\nendif"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Allow equivalent pseudocode expressions. Variables must not have speech marks around them. Correct completed code is:\\n\\n```\\nif num1 > num2 then\\n  print(num1)\\nelse\\n  print(num2)\\nendif\\n```\\n\\nEach blank is position-locked and must be marked against its intended position only: blank 1 (before `num1 >`) must be `if`; blank 2 (after `num1 >`) must be `num2`; blank 3 (inside the if branch) must be `print(num1)`; blank 4 (inside the else branch) must be `print(num2)`. Do not award a mark for a correct item placed in the wrong blank.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Blank 1 (before `num1 >`): if","marks":1},{"criteria":"Blank 2 (after `num1 >`): num2","marks":1},{"criteria":"Blank 3 (if branch): print(num1)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Blank 4 (else branch): print(num2)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"15(b)","parent_question":15,"topic":"doubling-loop-algorithm","marks":5,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A second program needs to perform the following tasks:\\n- Input a number from the user\\n- Double the number input and print the result\\n- Repeat bullets 1 and 2 until the user enters a number less than 0.\\n\\nWrite an algorithm for this program."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example 1 (structured English):\\n\\n```\\nstore 10 in number\\nwhile number is greater than or equal to 0\\ndo the following:\\n  Take input from the user, store in number\\n  Multiply number by 2\\n  Output number\\n```\\n\\nExample 2 (pseudocode):\\n\\n```\\nwhile number >= 0\\n  number = input()\\n  output(number * 2)\\n```\\n\\nIgnore non-initialisation of value used in condition for loop.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"use of condition controlled loop (while or do/until)","marks":1},{"criteria":"checking condition of number larger than or equal to 0","marks":1},{"criteria":"Input number from user within loop (FT if no loop)","marks":1},{"criteria":"multiply number input by 2","marks":1},{"criteria":"output value in number","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"16","parent_question":16,"topic":"complex-boolean-cinema","marks":3,"command_word":"Complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A cinema uses the following criteria to decide if a customer is allowed to see a film that has a 15 rating:\\n\\nCustomers have to be 15 years of age or older to see the film. They also need to either have a ticket or have the money to buy a ticket.\\n\\nThe table shows the inputs to the system that will output whether the customer can watch the film."},{"type":"table","headers":["Input","Criteria (True / False)"],"rows":[["A","The customer is 15 or over"],["B","The customer has a ticket"],["C","The customer has the money to buy a ticket"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following algorithm to output whether the customer is allowed to see the film or not."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"A = input(\\"Is the customer 15 or over?\\")\\nB = input(\\"Does the customer have a ticket?\\")\\nC = input(\\"Does the customer have money to buy a ticket?\\")"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\n\\n```\\nif A AND (B OR C) then\\n  print(\\"allowed\\")\\nelse\\n  print(\\"not allowed\\")\\nendif\\n```\\n\\nAccept answers where inputs are given as strings e.g.:\\nif A == \\"Yes\\" AND (B == \\"Yes\\" OR C == \\"Yes\\") then...","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Logically compares A AND // correct nested IF","marks":1},{"criteria":"...B OR C // correct sequential IF","marks":1},{"criteria":"Output in both cases (with attempt at selection)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"17(a)(i)","parent_question":17,"topic":"car-validation-algorithm","marks":5,"command_word":"Write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A car dealership uses a computer system to record details of the cars that it has for sale. Each car has a make, model, age and number of miles driven.\\n\\nThe car dealership only sells cars that have fewer than 10 000 miles and are 5 years old or less.\\n\\nWrite an algorithm that will:\\n- ask the user to enter the number of miles and the age of a car\\n- validate the input to check that only sensible values that are in the given range are entered\\n- output True if valid data has been entered or False if invalid data has been entered."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\n\\n```\\nmiles = input(\\"enter miles driven\\")\\nage = input(\\"enter age of car\\")\\nvalid = True\\nif miles > 10000 or miles < 0 then\\n  valid = False\\nelseif age > 5 or age < 0 then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nprint(valid)\\n```\\n\\nBP2 and 3 must check for both ends of range – must check that input data is not negative. Allow FT for BP4 if already penalised under BP2 and/or 3 and output is otherwise correct.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Miles and age input separately","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks for valid mileage","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks for valid age","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks both are greater than / greater than equal to zero","marks":1},{"criteria":"correctly outputs both True and False","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"17(a)(ii)","parent_question":17,"topic":"car-validation-test-data","marks":3,"command_word":"Identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The validation routine from part (i) must be tested with normal, erroneous and boundary test data.\\n\\nIdentify suitable test data for each type of test."},{"type":"table","headers":["","Miles","Age"],"rows":[["Normal","",""],["Erroneous","",""],["Boundary","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Specific data must be given, not a description.\\n\\nNormal: miles (0 – 9,999), age (0 - 5). e.g. Normal 7,000 / 3.\\nErroneous: miles (less than 0, larger than 9,999), age (less than 0 / more than 5) // non-numeric data. e.g. Erroneous 12,000 / 7.\\nBoundary: miles (-1/0 / 9,999 / 10,000), age (-1/0 / 5/6). e.g. Boundary 10,000 / 5.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Normal: miles 0-9999, age 0-5","marks":1},{"criteria":"Erroneous: miles out of range, age out of range or non-numeric","marks":1},{"criteria":"Boundary: miles -1/0/9999/10000, age -1/0/5/6","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"17(a)(iii)","parent_question":17,"topic":"iterative-testing","marks":1,"command_word":"Identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify when iterative testing is performed."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Iterative testing is performed during