s other logical errors.","Ignore capitals.","Do not accept \`*\` or additional fields for BP1.","Spelling must be accurate (e.g. not \`TblResults\`).","No spaces in field names; penalise obvious spaces once then FT.","Allow quotation marks around field names, table name and \`11\`.","Accept \`==\` for BP4 (invalid SQL but works in some environments)."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"TeamName only in first space","marks":1},{"criteria":"TblResult in second space","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE keyword","marks":1},{"criteria":"YearGroup = 11","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2ei","parent_question":2,"topic":"abstraction in program design","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Abstraction and decomposition have been used in the design of the sports day program."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify one way that abstraction has been used in the design of this program."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Must be applicable to this program (in the context of students and a sports day), not a generic description of what abstraction is. Give benefit of the doubt where unclear. Examples: 'focus on student names and events'; 'ignore data such as students' favourite subjects'; 'store year groups instead of ages or DOB'; 'shows student IDs instead of full student details'.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Any example of simplification / removing data or focussing on data (in the design), applicable to the sports day context","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2eii","parent_question":2,"topic":"decomposition in program design","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify one way that decomposition has been used in the design of this program."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Must be applicable to this program, not a generic description of what decomposition is. Give BOD where unclear. Do not give answers discussing splitting into fields (e.g. split into StudentID, YearGroup, etc). BOD if answer discusses one table but suggests other tables 