uotation marks, == for assignment, spaces in variable names) penalise once then FT. 'input' cannot be used as a variable name.\\n\\nExample 1:\\nhighscore = 0\\nwhile team != \\"stop\\"\\n  team = input(\\"enter team name\\")\\n  score = input(\\"enter score\\")\\n  if score > highscore then\\n    highscore = score\\n    highteam = team\\n  endif\\nendwhile\\nprint(highscore)\\nprint(highteam)\\n\\nExample 2 (alternative):\\nscores = []\\nteams = []\\nwhile team != \\"stop\\"\\n  team = input(\\"enter team name\\")\\n  score = input(\\"enter score\\")\\n  scores.append(score)\\n  teams.append(team)\\nendwhile\\nhighscore = max(scores)\\nhighteam = teams[scores.index(highscore)]\\nprint(highscore)\\nprint(highteam)","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input team name AND score and store / use separately","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at using iteration","marks":1},{"criteria":"...to enter team/score until 'stop' entered","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates highest score","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates winning team name","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs highest score and team name","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"3i","parent_question":3,"topic":"binary search trace","marks":3,"command_word":"show","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Show how a binary search will be used to find the number 10 in the following data set:"},{"type":"text","value":"1   2   5   6   7   10   20"}],"answer":{"guidance":"BP1 can be given for generic answer. BP2 and 3 must be linked to the data set given. For BP2, must remove 1, 2, 5 and 6 from the list if discussing individual numbers. Allow FT for BP3 if this is done incorrectly.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Compare to / pick out middle value (which is 6)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Discard only left side / retain only right side (because 6 < 10)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Compare to / pick out (middle value which is) 10","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"3ii","parent_question":3,"topic":"binary search prerequisite","marks":1,"command_word":"state","