_word":"design","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Drones flies goods around the country using drones.\\n\\nA text file is used to store pilot’s codes and date of birth.\\n\\nThe text file is named pilots.txt. The contents of some of this file is shown:"},{"type":"code","value":"JP670,17/05/1986\\nCC200,31/06/1980\\nSM720,01/04/1976\\nGC730,06/06/1978"},{"type":"text","value":"Design an algorithm to:\\n• Ask the user to input a pilot code and a date of birth\\n• Write these inputs to the pilots.txt text file"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"One mark per bullet point. Award BP4 for implicit closing of file (e.g. using `with...` in Python). Allow data to be written either by writing both values or by concatenating into one string with a separating comma."},{"type":"text","value":"Example answer:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"dronepilotData = open(\\"pilots.txt\\")\\npilotCode = input(\\"enter code\\")\\ndob = input(\\"enter date of birth\\")\\ndronepilotData.writeLine(pilotCode, dob)\\ndronepilotData.close()"}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Ask the user for two inputs and store/use these","marks":1},{"criteria":"Open pilots.txt (for write/append)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Write both inputs to opened text file","marks":1},{"criteria":"Close text file (implicit closing acceptable)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(b)","parent_question":7,"topic":"functions; 2D arrays; casting; selection","marks":6,"command_word":"create","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A pilot is allowed to fly a maximum of 9 hours per day. The pilot code and the hours flown for each flight in one day are stored in a 2D array of strings with the identifier journeys.\\n\\nThe data in journeys is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["","[0]","[1]"],"rows":[["[0]","\\"SM720\\"","\\"4.5\\""],["[1]","\\"GC730\\"","\\"3\\""],["[2]","\\"JP670\\"","\\"2\\""],["[3]","\\"GC730\\"","\\"3.5\\""],["[4]","\\"CC200\\"","\\"9\\""],["[5]","\\"RY320\\"","\\"12\\""]]},{"type":"text","value":"The value of journeys[3,1] is \\"3.5\\".\\n\\nCreate a function, pilotValid(), that:\\n• takes a pilot code as a parameter\\n• uses the 2D array journeys to calculate the number of hours that the pilot has flown\\n• returns valid if the pilot has flown 9 hours or fewer or warning if the pilot has flown for more than 9 hours\\n• uses casting where needed.\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction pilotValid(pilotCode)\\n  total = 0\\n  status = \\"\\"\\n  for i = 0 to 5\\n    if journeys[i,0] == pilotCode then\\n      temp = float(journeys[i,1])\\n      total = total + temp\\n    endif\\n  next i\\n  if total > 9 then\\n    status = \\"warning\\"\\n  else\\n    status = \\"valid\\"\\n  endif\\n  return status\\nendfunction\\n\\nDo not allow casting to integer; data includes decimal places.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Function header pilotValid() with at least one parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks array element [i,0] for each item / iterates array","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates total hours","marks":1},{"criteria":"Casting to float / real","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks if 9 hours or fewer and returns a value","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns \\"warning\\" and \\"valid\\" correctly","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8","parent_question":8,"topic":"operators; comparison; arithmetic","marks":4,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Tick (✓) one box in each row to identify if each operator is a comparison operator or an arithmetic operator."},{"type":"table","headers":["Operator","Comparison","Arithmetic"],"rows":[["`==`","",""],["`+`","",""],["`DIV`","",""],["`>`","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"== Comparison; + Arithmetic; DIV Arithmetic; > Comparison.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"== = Comparison","marks":1},{"criteria":"+ = Arithmetic","marks":1},{"criteria":"DIV = Arithmetic","marks":1},{"criteria":"> = Comparison","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9(i)","parent_question":9,"topic":"input validation; selection; iteration","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A player enters a code at the beginning of a computer game. The code is three characters long.\\nThe code sets the level of the game. The game has three levels.\\n\\nA variable level is assigned a value based on the code entered."},{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm that:\\n• asks the user to enter a three-character code\\n• repeats the previous step if the code is not 3 characters long\\n• if the code entered is SVA, assigns the value 2 to level\\n• if the code entered is UTV, assigns the value 3 to level\\n• assigns the value 1 to level if any other three-character code is entered."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nlevel = 0\\ncode = \\"\\"\\nwhile code.length != 3 then\\n   code = input(\\"enter a 3 character code\\")\\nendwhile\\nswitch code :\\n   case \\"SVA\\":\\n     level = 2\\n   case \\"UTV\\":\\n     level = 3\\n   default:\\n     level = 1\\nendswitch","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input code from user and store/use","marks":1},{"criteria":"Repeat for non-three character codes","marks":1},{"criteria":"Check for one code","marks":1},{"criteria":"Set level appropriately for that code","marks":1},{"criteria":"Check for and set level for 2nd code","marks":1},{"criteria":"Set level to 1 for any other 3 character code","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9(ii)","parent_question":9,"topic":"functions; parameters; return values","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"When a player completes a level, they move to the next level.\\n\\nOnce level 3 is completed, the game starts again at level 1.\\n\\nWrite a function called nextlevel() that:\\n• takes the current level as a parameter\\n• works out the integer value of the next level the player moves to\\n• returns the integer value."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction nextlevel(oldlevel)\\n    if oldlevel == 3 then\\n        return 1\\n    else\\n        return oldlevel + 1\\n    endif\\nend function\\n\\nAccept correct use of MOD.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"function nextlevel() defined with at least one parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns parameter plus 1","marks":1},{"criteria":"Except when parameter is 3, then returns 1","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9(iii)","parent_question":9,"topic":"function calls; output","marks":1,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete the line of code to output the value returned from the function `nextlevel()` when the integer value 3 is passed in as a parameter."},{"type":"code","value":"print(____(____))"}],"answer":{"guidance":"print(nextlevel(3))","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"print(nextlevel(3))","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(a)","parent_question":10,"topic":"testing; test plans; boundary/normal/erroneous","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Drones flies goods around the country using drones.\\n\\nA pilot’s flying experience is validated. An algorithm checks that the experience is between 0 and 20 years."},{"type":"code","value":"exp = input(\\"Enter number of years\\")\\nif exp >= 0 and exp <= 20 then\\n    print(True)\\nelse\\n    print(False)\\nendif"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete this test plan for the algorithm."},{"type":"table","headers":["Experience in years","Type of test","Expected output"],"rows":[["","Normal","True"],["20","Boundary",""],["32","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Row 1 experience: any value between 0 and 20 (e.g. 4). Row 2 expected output: True. Row 3 type of test: Invalid / Erroneous. Row 3 expected output: False.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Any value between 0 and 20 (e.g. 4)","marks":1},{"criteria":"True (expected output for 20)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Invalid / erroneous (type of test for 32)","marks":1},{"criteria":"False (expected output for 32)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(b)(i)","parent_question":10,"topic":"selection; calculation; input","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Pilots are paid a set amount each day. Pilots also get an additional payment for each mile they have flown that day. These payments are shown in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Flying experience","Pay per day","Pay per mile"],"rows":[["Fewer than 2 years","£120.00","£0.45"],["2 years to 5 years inclusive","£150.00","£0.65"],["More than 5 years","£180.00","£0.85"]]},{"type":"text","value":"For example, a pilot with 3 years’ experience who flies 100 miles in one day will receive a total of £215.00 pay.\\nThis is calculated in the following way:\\n• £150.00 pay for the day\\n• £65.00 additional payment (£0.65 pay per mile x 100 miles)\\n• Add £150.00 and £65.00 together to get £215.00 total pay"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the algorithm to:\\n• Calculate the total pay for the pilot for that day\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","value":"experience = input(\\"Enter years of experience\\")\\nmiles = input(\\"Enter miles flown\\")\\ntotalPay = 0\\n\\n# Write your algorithm here to set totalPay based on experience\\n# (use selection: < 2 years, 2 to 5 years, more than 5 years)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nprint(totalPay)"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nif experience < 2 then\\n    totalPay = 120+(0.45*miles)\\nelseif experience <= 5 then\\n    totalPay = 150+(0.65*miles)\\nelse\\n    totalPay = 180+(0.85*miles)\\nend if","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Attempt at using selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for pilots with less than 2 years experience","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for pilots with 2 to 5 years experience (must include both 2 and 5)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for pilots with more than 5 years experience","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(b)(ii)","parent_question":10,"topic":"functions; parameters; refactoring","marks":2,"command_word":"refine","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The programmer decides to make a function to calculate the total pay for the pilot.\\nThe function is called calculatePay().\\n\\nThe function takes the values for experience and miles as two parameters and returns the total pay for the pilot.\\n\\nRefine the algorithm to use this function and output the pay for the pilot.\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","value":"experience = input(\\"Enter years of experience\\")\\nmiles = input(\\"Enter miles flown\\")\\n____ = calculatePay(____, ____)\\nprint( totalPay )"}],"answer":{"guidance":"totalPay = calculatePay(experience, miles)","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"totalPay (on left of assignment)","marks":1},{"criteria":"(experience, miles) as parameters (either order)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"11","parent_question":11,"topic":"iteration; condition-controlled loops; insertion sort","marks":2,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An insertion sort is one type of sorting algorithm.\\n\\nA student has written a pseudocode algorithm to perform an insertion sort on a 1D array names."},{"type":"code","value":"names = [\\"Kareem\\", \\"Sarah\\", \\"Zac\\", \\"Sundip\\", \\"Anika\\"]\\nfor count = 1 to names.length - 1\\n  pos = count\\n  while (pos > 0 and names[pos] < names[pos - 1])\\n    temp = names[pos]\\n    names[pos] = names[pos - 1]\\n    names[pos - 1] = temp\\n    pos = pos - 1\\n  endwhile\\nnext count"},{"type":"text","value":"An insertion sort contains a nested loop; a loop within a loop. In this pseudocode algorithm the outer loop is a count-controlled loop and the inner loop is a condition-controlled loop.\\n\\nExplain why the inner loop needs to be a condition-controlled loop."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Max 1 from each section. Reason: do not know how many iterations/swaps needed / do not know how many times a condition-controlled loop will need to run. Condition: repeats while condition is true/false / repeats while value in [pos-1] is larger than value in [pos] / will swap until in correct position.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Do not know (at run time) how many iterations/swaps needed","marks":1},{"criteria":"Condition-controlled loop runs while/until a condition is true/false (e.g. while swap needed / until in correct position)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12(a)","parent_question":12,"topic":"selection; Boolean logic; procedure calls","marks":4,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An alarm has an algorithm that decides whether to sound the alarm by checking the data that is stored in the following three variables.\\n• SystemArmed\\n• DoorSensorActive\\n• WindowSensorActive\\n\\nThe alarm will only sound when the alarm has been activated and one or both of the door and window sensors are activated. When the system needs to sound the alarm it calls the pre-written procedure SoundAlarm()\\n\\nWrite a program that checks the data in the variables and calls SoundAlarm() when appropriate.\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nif SystemArmed then\\n  if DoorSensorActive then\\n    SoundAlarm()\\n  else if WindowSensorActive then\\n    SoundAlarm()\\n  endif\\nendif\\n\\nAlternative: if SystemArmed and (DoorSensorActive or WindowSensorActive) then SoundAlarm() endif. Brackets/parentheses essential due to operator precedence.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Attempt at using selection / condition-controlled loop","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checking if system armed / while system armed","marks":1},{"criteria":"If Door Sensor active OR Window Sensor active (both checks required)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calling SoundAlarm correctly","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12(b)(i)","parent_question":12,"topic":"string concatenation","marks":1,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An alarm system has multiple sensors. Each type of sensor has a code. The code for each sensor is given in the table:"},{"type":"table","headers":["Code","Sensor"],"rows":[["MS","Motion sensor"],["DS","Door sensor"],["WS","Window sensor"]]},{"type":"text","value":"A program is written to reset the sensors. The program:\\n• asks the user to enter the code for the sensor they want to reset\\n• calls the prewritten function CheckSensorCode() to check whether the code entered is a valid code\\n• the sensor number is read as input if the code is valid and the function ResetSensor() is called for the sensor"},{"type":"code","value":"01 sensorType = input(\\"Enter code of the type of sensor to reset\\")\\n02 if(CheckSensorCode(sensorType)) then\\n03   sensorNumber = input(\\" Please input the number of the sensor to reset\\")\\n04   sensorID = sensorType + sensorNumber\\n05   ResetSensor(sensorID)\\n06 endif"},{"type":"text","value":"Give the line number where there is concatenation."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Line 04 joins together sensorType and sensorNumber, assigning the concatenated result to sensorID.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Line 04","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12(b)(ii)","parent_question":12,"topic":"variables; identifiers","marks":1,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the identifier of a variable used in the program."}],"answer":{"guidance":"sensorType / sensorNumber / sensorID. Do not penalise case, spacing or minor misspellings.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"sensorType, sensorNumber or sensorID","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12(b)(iii)","parent_question":12,"topic":"data types; return values; Boolean","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify the data type of the data returned by the function CheckSensorCode()"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Boolean. Accept Bool. Inferred from use in selection statement.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Boolean","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12(b)(iv)","parent_question":12,"topic":"function calls","marks":1,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the line number that contains a function call."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Line 01 / Line 02 / Line 03 / Line 05. Explicit calls are on lines 02 (CheckSensorCode) and 05 (ResetSensor). Many languages implement input as a function (lines 01 and 03).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Line 01, 02, 03 or 05","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12(b)(v)","parent_question":12,"topic":"programming constructs","marks":2,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify two programming constructs that have been used in the program."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Selection and Sequence. Ignore minor spelling errors. Do not accept examples (e.g. IF). Iteration is not used in this program.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"Sequence","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12(c)","parent_question":12,"topic":"procedures; file handling; parameters","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A program written in a high-level language is used to access the data from a database.\\nThis program has a procedure, SaveLogs(), that stores the data to an external text file.\\n\\nThe procedure SaveLogs():\\n• takes the string of data to be stored to the text file as a parameter\\n• takes the filename of the text file as a parameter\\n• stores the string of data to the text file.\\n\\nWrite the procedure SaveLogs()\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nprocedure SaveLogs(data, filename)\\n  logFile = open(filename)\\n  logFile.writeLine(data)\\n  logFile.close()\\nendprocedure","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Define procedure SaveLogs","marks":1},{"criteria":"With two valid parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"Open file (for write/append)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Using the file name passed in as parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Write data to file using data passed in as parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Close file","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12(d)(i)","parent_question":12,"topic":"casting; data types","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Security Services need to identify the total number of seconds the sensors have been activated on a specific date.\\n\\nThe data from the database table events is imported into the program written in a highlevel programming language.\\n\\nThe program stores the data in a two-dimensional (2D) string array with the identifier arrayEvents\\n\\nThe data to be stored is shown in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Date","SensorID","SensorType","Length"],"rows":[["05/02/2023","WS2","Window","38"],["05/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["06/02/2023","DS3","Door","1"],["06/02/2023","MS2","Motion","3"],["06/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["07/02/2023","WS1","Window","24"],["07/02/2023","DS1","Door","1"]]},{"type":"text","value":"In this table, the value of `events[1, 1]` contains `\\"MS1\\"`.\\n\\nAn array can only store data of one data type. Any non-string data must be converted to a string before storing in the array.\\n\\nIdentify the process that converts integer data to string data."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Casting / cast. Accept type casting. Do not accept conversion. Do not accept examples of casting.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Casting / cast","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"12(d)(ii)","parent_question":12,"topic":"iteration; 2D arrays; selection; accumulation","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write a program that:\\n• asks the user to input a date\\n• totals the number of seconds sensors have been activated on the date input\\n• outputs the calculated total in an appropriate message including the date, for example:\\nSensors were activated for 40 seconds on 05/02/2023\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\ntotal = 0\\ndate = input(\\"Please enter date\\")\\nfor count = 0 to events.length-1\\n  if events[0, count] == date then\\n    total = total + events[3,count]\\n  endif\\nnext count\\nprint(\\"There were \\" + total + \\" events on \\" + date)","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input date and store in variable / use directly","marks":1},{"criteria":"Access all seven events in array / loop for each event","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"Compare date input against date in array (element 0)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Adding length (element 3) from array to total if dates match","marks":1},{"criteria":"Output calculated total and date in appropriate message at the end","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"13(a)","parent_question":13,"topic":"selection; iteration; constructs","marks":4,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Tick (✓) one box in each row to identify whether the OCR Reference Language code given is an example of selection or iteration."},{"type":"table","headers":["OCR Reference Language code","Selection","Iteration"],"rows":[["```\\nfor i = 1 to 10\\n   print(i)\\nnext i\\n```","",""],["```\\nwhile score != 0\\n   playgame()\\nendwhile\\n```","",""],["```\\nif playerHit() then\\n   score = 0\\nendif\\n```","",""],["```\\nswitch bonus:\\n   case 0:\\n      score = 9\\n   case 1:\\n      score = 7\\n   case 2:\\n      score = 5\\nendswitch\\n```","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"One mark per correct row."},{"type":"list","items":["`for ... next` = Iteration","`while ... endwhile` = Iteration","`if ... endif` = Selection","`switch ... endswitch` = Selection"]},{"type":"text","value":"Accept any response (ticks, crosses, etc.) that clearly indicates the candidate\'s choice."}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"for = Iteration","marks":1},{"criteria":"while = Iteration","marks":1},{"criteria":"if = Selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"switch = Selection","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"13(b)","parent_question":13,"topic":"pseudocode; assignment; arithmetic","marks":1,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write pseudocode to increment a value held in a variable score by one."}],"answer":{"guidance":"score = score + 1 // score += 1 // score++. Do not accept score + 1 / score = +1. Accept valid structured English answers.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"score = score + 1 (or score += 1 / score++)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"14(i)","parent_question":14,"topic":"arithmetic operators","marks":2,"command_word":"state","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Jack’s program uses the addition ( + ) arithmetic operator. This adds together two numbers.\\n\\nState the purpose of each of the arithmetic operators in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Arithmetic operator","Purpose"],"rows":[["`*`",""],["`/`",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"* = Multiplication; / = Division. Accept floor / integer division / division with no remainder for / (Python v2.x).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"* = Multiplication","marks":1},{"criteria":"/ = Division","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"14(ii)","parent_question":14,"topic":"programming languages; translators; interpreters; compilers","marks":5,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete the description of programming languages and translators by writing the correct term from the box in each space."},{"type":"text","value":"Word box: continues, crashes, debugging, error, executable, high-level, interpreter, language, low-level, many, no, one, stops, with, without"},{"type":"text","value":"Jack writes his program in a ____ language. This needs to be translated into assembly or machine code before it can be executed. This is done using a translator.\\n\\nOne type of translator is an interpreter. This converts one line of code and then executes it, before moving to the next line. It ____ when an error is found, and when corrected continues running from the same position. This translator is helpful when debugging code.\\n\\nA second type of translator is a compiler. This converts all of the code and produces an error report. The code will not run until there are ____ errors.\\n\\nThe ____ file produced can be run ____ the compiler."}],"answer":{"guidance":"high-level; stops (or crashes); no; executable; without.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"high-level","marks":1},{"criteria":"stops (or crashes)","marks":1},{"criteria":"no","marks":1},{"criteria":"executable","marks":1},{"criteria":"without","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"15(a)(i)","parent_question":15,"topic":"validation; selection; Boolean logic","marks":5,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Customers at a hotel can stay between 1 and 5 (inclusive) nights and can choose between a basic room or a premium room.\\n\\nWhen a new booking is recorded, the details are entered into a program to validate the values. The following criteria are checked:\\n- `firstName` and `surname` are not empty\\n- `room` is either \\"basic\\" or \\"premium\\"\\n- `nights` is between 1 and 5 (inclusive).\\n\\nIf any invalid data is found \\"NOT ALLOWED\\" is displayed.\\nIf all data is valid \\"ALLOWED\\" is displayed.\\n\\nComplete the following program to validate the inputs.\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n- OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n- a high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"firstName = input(\\"Enter a first name\\")\\nsurname = input(\\"Enter a surname\\")\\nroom = input(\\"Enter basic or premium\\")\\nnights = input(\\"Enter between 1 and 5 nights\\")\\nstayComplete = False"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"*General Mark Scheme guidance*"},{"type":"text","value":"1 mark each, to max 5."},{"type":"list","items":["Checks that both `firstName` and `surname` are 