/double/numeric etc.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Stage: String (or equivalent e.g. text/varchar/char)","marks":1},{"criteria":"SetLength: Real / Float (or equivalent e.g. decimal/single/double/numeric)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(b)(i)","parent_question":1,"topic":"sub-programs (functions, parameters, return)","marks":4,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Tickets to the festival are £60 each. Visitors can buy multiple tickets. For example, a visitor buying 4 tickets would pay £240."},{"type":"text","value":"Write a function, calculatePrice() that:\\n• takes the number of tickets to be purchased as a parameter\\n• calculates and returns the total price to pay.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Section B so must be high level code. Example code:\\nfunction calculatePrice(num)\\n    price = num * 60\\n    return price\\nendfunction\\nAll code must be within function definition (if present). BP3 - if no parameter present, allow multiplying by sensible value. FT overwriting parameter. BP4 must be return; do not credit output/print. Accept multiple parameters passed in. Accept returning by assigning to function name (e.g. VB).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Function definition for calculatePrice()","marks":1},{"criteria":"...with parameter that is not overwritten","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculate price based on multiplying parameter (if present) by 60","marks":1},{"criteria":"...always return calculated price","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(b)(ii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"sub-programs (calling a function)","marks":2,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm that:\\n• uses the function calculatePrice() to find the price for a visitor buying 3 tickets\\n• stores the result in the variable totalPrice\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example code: totalPrice = calculatePrice(3). Do not accept == for assignment. Allow FT to BP2 only if sensible attempt at BP1. Allow multiple values passed in as long as 3 is one of the values. Do not accept definitions of a function - must be calling the existing function.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"calculatePrice(3) called (with 3 as parameter)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...return value assigned to totalPrice","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(c)(i)","parent_question":1,"topic":"arrays (1D) and trace tables","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The number of different music acts on each of the three stages is stored in the array `actNumbers`. Each index of the array represents one stage."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","0","1","2"],"rows":[["Data","10","14","6"]],"caption":"actNumbers"},{"type":"text","value":"This algorithm adds up the total number of acts on all three stages."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"01 count = 0\\n02 for x = 0 to 2\\n03   count = count + actNumbers[x]\\n04 next x\\n05 print(count)"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the trace table for the algorithm. You may not need to use all rows in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Line number","count","x","Output"],"rows":[["","","",""],["","","",""],["","","",""],["","","",""],["","","",""],["","","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Based on example data where actNumbers = [10, 14, 6]. Ignore line numbers - not required. Mark order of values. Values can be repeated in count and x columns, look at changes. FT for BP4 if incorrect answer calculated but output.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"count initially set to 0","marks":1},{"criteria":"count increases to 10, 24, 30 and no other changes","marks":1},{"criteria":"x goes from 0, 1, 2 (, 3) and no other changes","marks":1},{"criteria":"30 output and no other output","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(c)(ii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"arrays (1