ount is \\" + count) or equivalent with suitable separator and variable outside quotes","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(a)(i)","parent_question":2,"topic":"data types","marks":3,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Students take part in a sports day. The students are put into teams. Students gain points depending on their result and the year group they are in. The points are added to the team score. The team with the most points at the end of the sports day wins. Data about the teams and students is stored in a sports day program."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify the most appropriate data type for each variable used by the program. Each data type must be different."},{"type":"table","headers":["Variable","Example","Data type"],"rows":[["teamName","\\"Super-Team\\"",""],["studentYearGroup","11",""],["javelinThrow","18.2",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept alternative equivalent correct data types (e.g. single/double/decimal for BP3). Do not accept char for BP1. Each data type must be different.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"teamName: String","marks":1},{"criteria":"studentYearGroup: Integer","marks":1},{"criteria":"javelinThrow: Real / Float","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(a)(ii)","parent_question":2,"topic":"arrays (1D) and sub-programs (linear search function)","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The student names for a team are stored in an array with the identifier `theTeam`. An example of the data in this array is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","0","1","2","3","4","5"],"rows":[["Data","Ali","Eve","Ling","Nina","Sarah","Tom"]],"caption":"theTeam"},{"type":"text","value":"A linear search function is used to find whether a student is in the team. The function:\\n• takes a student name as a parameter\\n• returns `True` if the student name is in the array\\n• returns `False` if the student name is **not** in the array."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the design of an algorithm for the linear search function."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"function linearSearch(studentName)\\n  for count = 0 to ____\\n    if theTeam[____] == ____ then\\n      return ____\\n    endif\\n  next count\\n  return False\\nendfunction"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept 6 // theTeam.length() for BP1 (Python). Accept alternative length functions e.g. len(). Accept count = 5 for BP1. Accept \\"True\\" for BP4. Do not allow obvious spaces in variable names. Ignore capitalisation.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Upper bound: theTeam.length() - 1 // 5 (or equivalent)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Array index: count","marks":1},{"criteria":"Comparison value: studentName","marks":1},{"criteria":"Return value: True","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(b)","parent_question":2,"topic":"trace tables (selection, conditions)","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"This algorithm calculates the number of points a student gets for the distance they throw in the javelin:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"01 javelinThrow = input(\\"Enter distance\\")\\n02 yearGroup = input(\\"Enter year group\\")\\n03 if javelinThrow >= 20.0 then\\n04   score = 3\\n05 elseif javelinThrow >= 10.0 then\\n06   score = 2\\n07 else\\n08   score = 1\\n09 endif\\n10 if yearGroup != 11 then\\n11   score = score * 2\\n12 endif\\n13 print(\\"The score is\\", score)"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the trace table for the algorithm when a student in year 10 throws a distance of 14.3. You may not need to use all the rows in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Line number","javelinThrow","yearGroup","score","Output"],"rows":[["","","","",""],["","","","",""],["","","","",""],["","","","",""],["","","","",""],["","","","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Max 3 if in wrong order or additional (incorrect) changes. Penalise line numbers once then FT. Allow FT for BP4 for current value of score. BP4 must not include comma. Ignore superfluous spaces/quotation marks.","marks_breakd