:{"guidance":"No need to include decimals, e.g. accept 50. Ignore cm if given. Answer must be actual data (e.g. 50) and not description of data.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Normal: any value between 40 and 180 inclusive (e.g. 50)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Boundary: 40.0 // 180.0","marks":1},{"criteria":"Erroneous: any value less than 40 // greater than 180 // non-numeric value","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(d)","parent_question":2,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The individual results for each student in each event are stored in a database. The database table TblResult stores the times of students in the 100 m race. Some of the data is shown:"},{"type":"table","headers":["StudentID","YearGroup","TeamName","Time"],"rows":[["11GC1","11","Valiants",""],["10VE1","10","Super-Team","20.3"],["10SM1","10","Super-Team","19.7"],["11JP2","11","Champions","19.2"],["","","","19.65"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the SQL statement to show the Student ID and team name of all students who are in year group 11."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT StudentID, ____\\nFROM ____\\n____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Max 3 if not in correct order / includes other logical errors. Ignore capitals. Do not accept * or additional fields for BP1. Spelling must be accurate (e.g. not TblResults). Accept == for BP4.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"TeamName in first space","marks":1},{"criteria":"TblResult in second space","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE","marks":1},{"criteria":"YearGroup = 11","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2(e)(i)","parent_question":2,"topic":"abstraction (in program design)","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Abstraction and decomposition have been used in the design of the sports day program."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify one way that abstraction has been used in the design of this program."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Must be applicable to this program (