0\\nwhile team != \\"stop\\"\\n   team = input(\\"enter team name\\")\\n   score = input(\\"enter score\\")\\n   if score > highscore then\\n     highscore = score\\n     highteam = team\\n   endif\\nendwhile\\nprint(highscore)\\nprint(highteam)\\nAllow use of break to exit loop. Allow use of recursive function(s) for BP2/3. Assume variables are 0/empty if not initialised. Allow arrays/lists or max/sum functions. FT for BP6.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input team name AND score and store/use separately","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at using iteration","marks":1},{"criteria":"...to enter team/score until \\"stop\\" entered","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates highest score","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates winning team name","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs highest score and team name","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"3(a)","parent_question":3,"topic":"string manipulation (length, upper, left, right, casting)","marks":3,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The variable `message` is assigned a value."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"message = \\"abcd1234\\""},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the table to show the output when each statement executes. The first output has been completed for you."},{"type":"table","headers":["Statement","Output"],"rows":[["print(message.length)","8"],["print(message.upper)",""],["print(message.left(4))",""],["print(int(message.right(4))*2)",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Case must be correct but BOD if ambiguous. Allow quotation marks in answer. 1 mark for each output.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"print(message.upper) -> ABCD1234 (upper case)","marks":1},{"criteria":"print(message.left(4)) -> abcd (lower case)","marks":1},{"criteria":"print(int(message.right(4))*2) -> 2468","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"3(b)","parent_question":3,"topic":"string manipulation (concatenation)","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm in pseudocode to:\\n• store \\"Hello\\" in the variable word1\\n• store \\"Everyone\\" in the variable word2\\n• concatenate word1 and word2 to store \\"HelloEveryone\\" in the variable message"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nword1 = \\"Hello\\"\\nword2 = \\"Everyone\\"\\nmessage = word1 + word2\\nAccept & / + / . etc as valid methods of concatenation. Allow use of sensible concatenation functions e.g. concat(). Do not allow commas. Do not allow == for assigning value. Do not allow spaces in variable names. Reasonable attempt at BP2 needed to access BP3.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Storing both strings correctly in word1 and word2","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correct concatenation (word1 then word2)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...storing in variable message","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"4(a)","parent_question":4,"topic":"file handling (open/write/close)","marks":4,"command_word":"design","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Drones flies goods around the country using drones. A text file is used to store pilot\'s codes and date of birth. The text file is named `pilots.txt`. The contents of some of this file is shown:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"JP670,17/05/1986\\nCC200,31/06/1980\\nSM720,01/04/1976\\nGC730,06/06/1978"},{"type":"text","value":"Design an algorithm to:\\n• Ask the user to input a pilot code and a date of birth\\n• Write these inputs to the `pilots.txt` text file"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"One mark per bullet point. Award BP4 for implicit closing of file (e.g. using `with...` in Python). Allow data to be written either by writing both values or by concatenating into one string with a separating comma."},{"type":"text","value":"Example answer:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"dronepilotData = open(\\"pilots.txt\\")\\npilotCode = input(\\"enter code\\")\\ndob = input(\\"enter date of birth\\")\\ndronepilotData.writeLine(pilotCode, dob)\\ndronepilotData.close()"}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Ask the user for two inputs and store/use these","marks":1},{"criteria":"Open pilots.txt (for write/append)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Write both inputs to opened text file","marks":1},{"criteria":"Close text file (implicit closing acceptable)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"4(b)","parent_question":4,"topic":"2D arrays and sub-programs (function with casting)","marks":6,"command_word":"create","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A pilot is allowed to fly a maximum of 9 hours per day. The pilot code and the hours flown for each flight in one day are stored in a 2D array of strings with the identifier `journeys`. The data in `journeys` is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","Column [0]","Column [1]"],"rows":[["[0]","\\"SM720\\"","\\"4.5\\""],["[1]","\\"GC730\\"","\\"3\\""],["[2]","\\"JP670\\"","\\"2\\""],["[3]","\\"GC730\\"","\\"3.5\\""],["[4]","\\"CC200\\"","\\"9\\""],["[5]","\\"RY320\\"","\\"12\\""]],"caption":"journeys"},{"type":"text","value":"The value of `journeys[3,1]` is `\\"3.5\\"`."},{"type":"text","value":"Create a function, pilotValid(), that:\\n• takes a pilot code as a parameter\\n• uses the 2D array journeys to calculate the number of hours that the pilot has flown\\n• returns valid if the pilot has flown 9 hours or fewer or warning if the pilot has flown for more than 9 hours\\n• uses casting where needed.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction pilotValid(pilotCode)\\n  total = 0\\n  status = \\"\\"\\n  for i = 0 to 5\\n    if journeys[i,0] == pilotCode then\\n      temp = float(journeys[i,1])\\n      total = total + temp\\n    endif\\n  next i\\n  if total > 9 then\\n    status = \\"warning\\"\\n  else\\n    status = \\"valid\\"\\n  endif\\n  return status\\nendfunction\\nDo not allow casting to integer for BP4; data shows decimal places. Allow FT for BP5 and BP7. Max 6 marks.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Function header pilotValid() with (at least one) parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks array element [i,0] for each item, calculates total","marks":1},{"criteria":"Casting to float / real","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks if 9 hours or fewer","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns a value","marks":1},{"criteria":"...returns \\"warning\\" and \\"valid\\" correctly","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(i)","parent_question":5,"topic":"iteration, selection, string length","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A player enters a code at the beginning of a computer game. The code is three characters long. The code sets the level of the game. The game has three levels. A variable level is assigned a value based on the code entered."},{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm that:\\n• asks the user to enter a three-character code\\n• repeats the previous step if the code is not 3 characters long\\n• if the code entered is SVA, assigns the value 2 to level\\n• if the code entered is UTV, assigns the value 3 to level\\n• assigns the value 1 to level if any other three-character code is entered."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nlevel = 0\\ncode = \\"\\"\\nwhile code.length != 3 then\\n  code = input(\\"enter a 3 character code\\")\\nendwhile\\nswitch code :\\n  case \\"SVA\\":\\n    level = 2\\n  case \\"UTV\\":\\n    level = 3\\n  default:\\n    level = 1\\nendswitch\\nAlternative with if/elseif/else also accepted.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input code from user and store/use","marks":1},{"criteria":"Repeat for non-three character codes","marks":1},{"criteria":"Check for one code (SVA)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...and set level appropriately (level = 2 for SVA)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Check for and set level for 2nd code (UTV -> level = 3)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Set level to 1 for any other 3 character code","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(ii)","parent_question":5,"topic":"sub-programs (function with parameter and return)","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"When a player completes a level, they move to the next level. Once level 3 is completed, the game starts again at level 1."},{"type":"text","value":"Write a function called nextlevel() that:\\n• takes the current level as a parameter\\n• works out the integer value of the next level the player moves to\\n• returns the integer value."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction nextlevel(oldlevel)\\n  if oldlevel == 3 then\\n    return 1\\n  else\\n    return oldlevel + 1\\n  endif\\nend function\\nAccept correct use of MOD for BP2 and 3. Allow FT for BP3 if value output/calculated but not returned.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"function nextlevel() defined with at least one parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns parameter plus 1","marks":1},{"criteria":"...except for if parameter is 3, then returns 1","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(iii)","parent_question":5,"topic":"sub-programs (calling a function)","marks":1,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete the line of code to output the value returned from the function nextlevel() when the integer value 3 is passed in as a parameter."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"print(____(____))"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Allow other logically correct answers.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"print(nextlevel(3))","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(a)(i)","parent_question":6,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE with AND","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Drones flies goods around the country using drones. Details about the drones that pilots fly are stored in a database table called TblDrone. Some of the data stored in this table is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["DroneID","DroneType","Mileage","LastCheck"],"rows":[["001","Quadcopter","65 032","65 000"],["002","Quadcopter","32 128","21 000"],["003","Octocopter","98 021","98 000"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the SQL statement to display DroneID and Mileage for all Octocopter type drones that have a mileage of greater than 50 000 miles."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT ____\\n____ TblDrone\\nWHERE DroneType = \\"Octocopter\\" ____ Mileage ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept SELECT * or selection of additional fields for BP1.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"SELECT DroneID, Mileage","marks":1},{"criteria":"FROM","marks":1},{"criteria":"AND","marks":1},{"criteria":"> 50000","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(a)(ii)","parent_question":6,"topic":"flowchart (selection / comparison)","marks":2,"command_word":"complete","response_style":"annotate-image","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Drones must be checked every 10 000 miles. If the difference between Mileage and LastCheck is greater than 10 000 then the drone needs to be checked."},{"type":"text","value":"A flowchart shows the steps needed to check a drone. The flowchart outputs \\"Check\\" if the drone needs to be checked. The flowchart outputs \\"No Check\\" if the drone does not need to be checked."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the flowchart for the algorithm."},{"type":"image","kind":"diagram","src":"j277/topics/ocr/2.2.3_q6aii_drone_flowchart_canvas.png","alt_text":"Drone-check flowchart with the comparison condition and output labels left empty for the candidate to complete."}],"answer":{"guidance":"BP1 could be >, < or either in words. Ignore case and minor misspellings. BP2 (output) could be either way around depending on comparison for BP1.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"if Mileage - LastCheck > 10000 (correct comparison)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Output \\"Check\\" and \\"No Check\\" (or equivalent) correctly based on logical check","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(b)","parent_question":6,"topic":"random number generation and trace tables","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A pilot code is automatically generated when a new pilot joins the company. This algorithm generates a code for each pilot:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"01 a = input(\\"Enter first letter of first name\\")\\n02 b = input(\\"Enter first letter of second name\\")\\n03 c = random(1,100)\\n04 while c < 100\\n05   c = c * 10\\n06 endwhile\\n07 pilotCode = a + b + str(c)\\n08 print(pilotCode)"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the trace table for the given algorithm. Lines 01 to 03 have already been completed. You may not need to use all rows in the trace table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Line number","a","b","c","pilotCode","Output"],"rows":[["01","H","","","",""],["02","","K","","",""],["03","","","9","",""],["","","","","",""],["","","","","",""],["","","","","",""],["","","","","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Ignore additional lines that do not affect outcome. FT for missing or incorrect line numbers. FT for output based on incorrect tracing of loop. 1 mark per row.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"c = 90 on line 05","marks":1},{"criteria":"c = 900 on line 05","marks":1},{"criteria":"pilotCode = HK900 on line 07","marks":1},{"criteria":"HK900 output on line 08","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(c)(i)","parent_question":6,"topic":"selection and calculation","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Pilots are paid a set amount each day. Pilots also get an additional payment for each mile they have flown that day. These payments are shown in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Flying experience","Pay per day","Pay per mile"],"rows":[["Fewer than 2 years","£120.00","£0.45"],["2 years to 5 years inclusive","£150.00","£0.65"],["More than 5 years","£180.00","£0.85"]]},{"type":"text","value":"For example, a pilot with 3 years\' experience who flies 100 miles in one day will receive a total of £215.00 pay. This is calculated in the following way:\\n• £150.00 pay for the day\\n• £65.00 additional payment (£0.65 pay per mile x 100 miles)\\n• Add £150.00 and £65.00 together to get £215.00 total pay"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the algorithm to:\\n• Calculate the total pay for the pilot for that day\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"experience = input(\\"Enter years of experience\\")\\nmiles = input(\\"Enter miles flown\\")\\ntotalPay = 0\\n____\\nprint(totalPay)"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nif exp < 2 then\\n  totalPay = 120 + (0.45 * miles)\\nelseif exp <= 5 then\\n  totalPay = 150 + (0.65 * miles)\\nelse\\n  totalPay = 180 + (0.85 * miles)\\nend if\\nFT for BP4 only where a reasonable attempt at calculating pay has been made.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Attempt at using selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for pilots with less than 2 years experience","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for pilots with 2 to 5 years experience (must include both 2 and 5)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for pilots with more than 5 years experience","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(c)(ii)","parent_question":6,"topic":"sub-programs (using a function)","marks":2,"command_word":"refine","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The programmer decides to make a function to calculate the total pay for the pilot. The function is called calculatePay(). The function takes the values for experience and miles as two parameters and returns the total pay for the pilot. Refine the algorithm to use this function and output the pay for the pilot."},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"experience = input(\\"Enter years of experience\\")\\nmiles = input(\\"Enter miles flown\\")\\n\\n____ = calculatePay( ____ , ____ )\\n\\nprint( totalPay )"}],"answer":{"guidance":"totalPay = calculatePay(experience, miles). Order of parameters acceptable either way (experience, miles) or (miles, experience).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"totalPay (as assignment target)","marks":1},{"criteria":"(experience, miles) // (miles, experience) as parameters","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(a)","parent_question":7,"topic":"sub-programs (procedures, selection with Boolean)","marks":4,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An alarm has an algorithm that decides whether to sound the alarm by checking the data that is stored in the following three variables.\\n• SystemArmed\\n• DoorSensorActive\\n• WindowSensorActive"},{"type":"text","value":"The alarm will only sound when the alarm has been activated and one or both of the door and window sensors are activated. When the system needs to sound the alarm it calls the pre-written procedure SoundAlarm()."},{"type":"text","value":"Write a program that checks the data in the variables and calls SoundAlarm() when appropriate.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nif SystemArmed then\\n  if DoorSensorActive then\\n    SoundAlarm()\\n  else if WindowSensorActive then\\n    SoundAlarm()\\n  endif\\nendif\\nSelection could be done using IF, case, or any other sensible valid method. Allow True/False as strings. Only award BP4 if SoundAlarm correctly called/not called in every situation. Watch for precedence errors (use brackets for (Door OR Window)).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Attempt at using selection / condition controlled loop","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checking if system armed // while system armed","marks":1},{"criteria":"If Door Sensor active OR Window Sensor active (both checks required)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calling SoundAlarm correctly","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(b)","parent_question":7,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE with AND","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An alarm system has a log that stores a record each time a sensor is triggered. This is called an event. The record format is given in the table:"},{"type":"table","headers":["Fieldname","Description"],"rows":[["Date","The date the event happened"],["SensorID","The sensor that was activated"],["SensorType","The type of sensor that was activated – Door, Motion or Window"],["Length","The number of seconds the sensor was triggered (to the nearest second)"]]},{"type":"text","value":"The log is stored in a database table called events. The current contents of events is shown:"},{"type":"table","headers":["Date","SensorID","SensorType","Length"],"rows":[["05/02/2023","WS2","Window","38"],["05/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["06/02/2023","DS3","Door","1"],["06/02/2023","MS2","Motion","3"],["06/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["07/02/2023","WS1","Window","24"],["07/02/2023","DS1","Door","1"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Write an SQL statement to display the sensor IDs of the door sensors that have been triggered for more than 20 seconds."}],"answer":{"guidance":"SELECT SensorID\\nFROM events\\nWHERE Length > 20 AND SensorType = \\"Door\\"\\nMax 2 if out of order or anything extra that affects the output. BP1 can select multiple fields as long as SensorID is included. \\"door\\" must be in quotation marks for BP3. Allow alternative WHERE clauses that are logically correct (e.g. WHERE length >= 21).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"SELECT SensorID (or SELECT *)","marks":1},{"criteria":"FROM events","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE Length > 20 AND SensorType = \\"Door\\" (or equivalent)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(c)","parent_question":7,"topic":"sub-programs (procedures) and file handling (open/write/close)","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A program written in a high-level language is used to access the data from a database. This program has a procedure, SaveLogs(), that stores the data to an external text file."},{"type":"text","value":"The procedure SaveLogs():\\n• takes the string of data to be stored to the text file as a parameter\\n• takes the filename of the text file as a parameter\\n• stores the string of data to the text file."},{"type":"text","value":"Write the procedure SaveLogs()\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nprocedure SaveLogs(data, filename)\\n  logFile = open(filename)\\n  logFile.writeLine(data)\\n  logFile.close()\\nendprocedure\\nMust be clear that answer is a procedure definition. Allow function definition. If parameters overwritten, do not credit BP2 but FT for BP4 and 6. If code given outside of procedure, do not give BP4 and BP6.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Define procedure SaveLogs","marks":1},{"criteria":"...with two valid parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"Open file (for write/append)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...using the file name passed in as parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Write data to file using the data passed in as parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Close file","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(d)(i)","parent_question":7,"topic":"casting (integer to string)","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Security Services need to identify the total number of seconds the sensors have been activated on a specific date. The data from the database table events is imported into the program written in a high-level programming language. The program stores the data in a two-dimensional (2D) string array with the identifier arrayEvents."},{"type":"text","value":"The data to be stored is shown in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Date","SensorID","SensorType","Length"],"rows":[["05/02/2023","WS2","Window","38"],["05/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["06/02/2023","DS3","Door","1"],["06/02/2023","MS2","Motion","3"],["06/02/2023","MS1","Motion","2"],["07/02/2023","WS1","Window","24"],["07/02/2023","DS1","Door","1"]]},{"type":"text","value":"In this table, the value of events[1, 1] contains \\"MS1\\"."},{"type":"text","value":"An array can only store data of one data type. Any non-string data must be converted to a string before storing in the array."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify the process that converts integer data to string data."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept type casting. Do not accept conversion. Do not accept examples of casting.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Casting / cast (or type casting)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(d)(ii)","parent_question":7,"topic":"2D arrays, iteration, selection, running total","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write a program that:\\n• asks the user to input a date\\n• totals the number of seconds sensors have been activated on the date input\\n• outputs the calculated total in an appropriate message including the date, for example:"},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"Sensors were activated for 40 seconds on 05/02/2023"},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• A high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\ntotal = 0\\ndate = input(\\"Please enter date\\")\\nfor count = 0 to events.length-1\\n  if events[0, count] == date then\\n    total = total + events[3, count]\\n  endif\\nnext count\\nprint(\\"There were \\" + total + \\" events on \\" + date)\\nBP2 loop allow off by one errors, looping to array length or array length - 1. BP4/5 allow array reference as either column major or row major. Only give output mark if attempt made to calculate total within the algorithm. Must be 0 to 6, not 1 to 7.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Input date and store in variable / use directly","marks":1},{"criteria":"Access all seven (indexes 0 to 6) events in array // loop for each event in array","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"...to compare date input against date in array (element 0)","marks":1},{"criteria":"...adding length (element 3) from array to the total if dates match","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputting calculated total and date in appropriate message(s) at the end","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(a)(i)","parent_question":8,"topic":"data types (records)","marks":2,"command_word":"state","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Customers at a hotel can stay between 1 and 5 (inclusive) nights and can choose between a basic room or a premium room. A typical booking record is shown in the table:"},{"type":"table","headers":["Field","Value"],"rows":[["firstName","Amaya"],["surname","Taylor-Ling"],["nights","3"],["room","Premium"],["stayComplete","False"]]},{"type":"text","value":"State the most appropriate data type for the following fields:\\nNights\\nRoom"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Accept other valid data types from high-level languages (e.g. byte, short for integers). Do not accept descriptions (e.g. \\"whole number\\", \\"text\\"). Do not accept \\"character(s)\\" for string.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Nights: Integer","marks":1},{"criteria":"Room: String","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(a)(ii)","parent_question":8,"topic":"data types (Boolean)","marks":1,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the name of one field that could be stored as a Boolean data type."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Ignore spaces or misspelling as long as recognisable.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"stayComplete","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(a)(iii)","parent_question":8,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE","marks":4,"command_word":"rewrite","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Booking records are stored in a database table called TblBookings. The following SQL statement is written to display all customer bookings that stay more than one night."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT ALL\\nFROM TblBookings\\nIF Nights < 1"},{"type":"text","value":"The SQL statement is incorrect. Rewrite the SQL statement so that it is correct."}],"answer":{"guidance":"SELECT FirstName, Surname, Nights, Room, StayComplete // SELECT *\\nFROM TblBookings\\nWHERE Nights > 1 // Nights >= 2 // Nights BETWEEN 2 AND 5\\nOrder of fields for BP1 not important but must show all fields and be separated by commas. Spelling must be correct. Max 3 if in wrong order or if includes any extra invalid code.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"SELECT FirstName, Surname, Nights, Room, StayComplete (or SELECT *)","marks":1},{"criteria":"FROM TblBookings (unchanged, correct)","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE (replacing IF)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Nights > 1 (or Nights >= 2 / Nights BETWEEN 2 AND 5)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(b)(i)","parent_question":8,"topic":"input validation with Booleans","marks":5,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"When a new booking is recorded, the details are entered into a program to validate the values. The following criteria are checked:\\n• `firstName` and `surname` are not empty\\n• `room` is either \\"basic\\" or \\"premium\\"\\n• `nights` is between 1 and 5 (inclusive).\\nIf any invalid data is found \\"NOT ALLOWED\\" is displayed. If all data is valid \\"ALLOWED\\" is displayed."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following program to validate the inputs. You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"firstName = input(\\"Enter a first name\\")\\nsurname = input(\\"Enter a surname\\")\\nroom = input(\\"Enter basic or premium\\")\\nnights = input(\\"Enter between 1 and 5 nights\\")\\nstayComplete = False\\n# Complete the program below"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"},{"type":"code","value":"valid = True\\nif firstname == \\"\\" or surname == \\"\\" then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif room != \\"basic\\" and room != \\"premium\\" then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif nights < 1 or nights > 5 then\\n  valid = False\\nendif\\nif valid then\\n  print(\\"ALLOWED\\")\\nelse\\n  print(\\"NOT ALLOWED\\")\\nendif"},{"type":"list","items":["Must have some attempt at all three checks to give output mark(s).","Check for nights must check both upper and lower limits.","Do not accept logically incorrect Boolean conditions such as `if firstname or surname == \\"\\"`."]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Checks that both firstname and surname are not empty","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks that room is either \\"basic\\" or \\"premium\\"","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks that nights is between 1 and 5 (inclusive)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"NOT ALLOWED\\" (or equivalent) if any of the 3 checks are invalid","marks":1},{"criteria":"Outputs \\"ALLOWED\\" (or equivalent) only if all three checks are valid","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(b)(ii)","parent_question":8,"topic":"test data (normal, boundary, erroneous)","marks":3,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following test plan to check whether the number of nights is validated correctly."},{"type":"table","headers":["Test data (number of nights)","Type of test","Expected output"],"rows":[["2","","ALLOWED"],["","Boundary","ALLOWED"],["","Erroneous / Invalid","NOT ALLOWED"]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"Allow other descriptions that mean normal (e.g. valid / typical / acceptable).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Normal (for test data 2)","marks":1},{"criteria":"1 or 5 (boundary value; not 0 or 6 as says allowed)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Any numeric value except 1 to 5 // any non-numeric input (e.g. 7 or \\"bananas\\")","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(c)(i)","parent_question":8,"topic":"sub-programs (function with multiple parameters)","marks":4,"command_word":"create","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A Basic room costs £60 each night. A Premium room costs £80 each night."},{"type":"text","value":"Create a function, newPrice(), that takes the number of nights and the type of room as parameters, calculates and returns the price to pay. You do not have to validate these parameters."},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction newPrice(nights, room)\\n  if room == \\"basic\\" then\\n    price = 60 * nights\\n  elseif room == \\"premium\\" then\\n    price = 80 * nights\\n  endif\\n  return price\\nendfunction\\nBP1 must be clear that a new function is being defined. Allow FT for subsequent marks if not present. If inputs used instead of parameters, FT for BP3. Must return (not output) value.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Function header for newPrice","marks":1},{"criteria":"...taking (at least) two parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"...correctly calculates price based on parameters within function","marks":1},{"criteria":"...returns this calculated price","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(c)(ii)","parent_question":8,"topic":"sub-programs (calling a function)","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write program code, that uses newPrice(), to output the price of staying in a Premium room for 5 nights."},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"e.g. print(newPrice(\\"premium\\", 5)) or x = newPrice(5, \\"premium\\"); print(x). Order of parameters not important. \\"premium\\" must use string delimiters. Do not allow function definitions for BP1.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Call function newPrice","marks":1},{"criteria":"...with (\\"premium\\", 5) as parameters","marks":1},{"criteria":"Output returned value","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(d)","parent_question":8,"topic":"iteration, selection, input/output","marks":6,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A hotel car park charges £4 per hour. If the car is electric, this price is halved to £2 per hour."},{"type":"text","value":"Write an algorithm to:\\n• take as input the number of hours the user has parked and whether their car is electric or not\\n• calculate and output the total price\\n• repeat continually until the user enters 0 hours.\\nYou must use either:\\n• OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n• a high level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nwhile hours != 0\\n  hours = input(\\"Enter hours\\")\\n  electric = input(\\"enter Y for electric or N\\")\\n  if electric == \\"Y\\" then\\n    price = hours * 2\\n  elseif electric == \\"N\\" then\\n    price = hours * 4\\n  endif\\n  print(price)\\nendwhile\\nInitialisation of price and hours not necessary. BP5 must include all points attempted. BP6 can be given as FT even if BP5 (loop) is in the wrong place.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Inputs hours AND electric (two separate inputs), storing or using these","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks if car is electric (IF/Select statement)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correctly calculates and outputs price (hours * 2 // price / 2) for electric","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correctly calculates and outputs price (hours * 4 // electric price * 2) for non-electric","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at repetition of BP1 to 4","marks":1},{"criteria":"...until 0 hours entered","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9","parent_question":9,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE","marks":3,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The database table Results stores the results for each student in each of their chosen subjects."},{"type":"table","headers":["StudentName","Subject","Grade"],"rows":[["Alistair","English","3"],["Jaxon","Art","5"],["Alex","Art","4"],["Anna","French","7"],["Ismaael","Art","9"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the SQL query to return all of the fields for the students who take Art."},{"type":"code","language":"sql","value":"SELECT ____\\nFROM ____\\nWHERE ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Correct Answer Only. Accept SELECT *.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"SELECT StudentName, Subject, Grade (or SELECT *)","marks":1},{"criteria":"FROM Results","marks":1},{"criteria":"WHERE Subject = \\"Art\\"","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10","parent_question":10,"topic":"sub-programs (calling a function and storing return value)","marks":2,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A cinema uses the following criteria to decide if a customer is allowed to see a film that has a 15 rating: Customers have to be 15 years of age or older to see the film. They also need to either have a ticket or have the money to buy a ticket."},{"type":"text","value":"The table shows the inputs to the system that will output whether the customer can watch the film."},{"type":"table","headers":["Input","Criteria (True / False)"],"rows":[["A","The customer is 15 or over"],["B","The customer has a ticket"],["C","The customer has the money to buy a ticket"]]},{"type":"text","value":"The cinema has three screens: \\"Red\\", \\"Black\\" and \\"Yellow\\". The function freeseats() counts how many seats are available in each screen. The name of the screen is passed in as a string parameter and the number of free seats is returned as an integer."},{"type":"text","value":"Write code using the function freeseats() to find the number of seats available in screen Red and assign this to a variable with identifier redseats."}],"answer":{"guidance":"redseats = freeseats(\\"Red\\"). \\"Red\\" must use suitable string delimiters (e.g. speech marks) if directly passing the string. Do not penalise case.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"freeseats called with \\"Red\\"","marks":1},{"criteria":"...returned value assigned to variable redseats","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"11(a)","parent_question":11,"topic":"SQL SELECT/FROM/WHERE (multiple choice)","marks":3,"command_word":"tick","content":[{"type":"text","value":"OCR Tech is an online shop that sells electronics such as TVs and game consoles."},{"type":"text","value":"Items for sale are stored in the database table `tblStock`. An extract of this table is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["ItemCode","ItemName","Price (£)","Stock"],"rows":[["GSC5","GameStation5 console","249.99","102"],["TV4K