he algorithm."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"function checkdiscount(price, code)\\n  newprice = price\\n  size = len(discount) – 1\\n  for x = 0 to ____\\n    if discount[x,0] == ____ then\\n      newprice = ____ – discount[____]\\n    endif\\n  next x\\n  ____\\nendfunction"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Example:\\nfunction checkdiscount(price, code)\\n  newprice = price\\n  size = len(discount)-1\\n  for x = 0 to size\\n    if discount[x,0] == code then\\n      newprice = price – discount[x,1]\\n    endif\\n  next\\n  return newprice\\nendfunction\\nOne mark per bullet point, in the correct place.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Upper bound: size // len(discountcodes)-1","marks":1},{"criteria":"Comparison value: code","marks":1},{"criteria":"Subtraction base: price // newprice","marks":1},{"criteria":"Discount index: [x,1] // [x][1]","marks":1},{"criteria":"return newprice // checkdiscount = newprice","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"11(b)(ii)","parent_question":11,"topic":"variables (identifying)","marks":2,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The function design from part (i) is shown below."},{"type":"code","language":"erl","value":"function checkdiscount(price, code)\\n  newprice = price\\n  size = len(discount) - 1\\n  for x = 0 to [missing value]\\n    if discount[x,0] == [missing value] then\\n      newprice = [missing value] - discount[[missing value]]\\n    endif\\n  next x\\n  [missing statement]\\nendfunction"},{"type":"text","value":"Identify two variables used in this function design."},{"type":"text","value":"1: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"2: ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Do not penalise capitalisation. Accept price, code, discount.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Any one of: newprice / size / x (or price / code / discount)","marks":1},{"criteria":"A second one of: newprice / size / x (or price / code / discount)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"11(b)(iii)","parent_question":11,"topic":"sub-programs (using a function), i