her markings that indicate a choice has been made (e.g. a cross, etc).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Uses English-like keywords such as print and while = High-level","marks":1},{"criteria":"Must be translated before the processor can execute code = High-level","marks":1},{"criteria":"Code written is portable between different processors = High-level","marks":1},{"criteria":"Requires the programmer to understand the processor\'s registers and structure = Low-level","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2.5.1-8a","parent_question":8,"topic":"translators (need for translation)","marks":1,"command_word":"state","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A computer game is written in a high-level programming language.\\n\\nState why the computer needs to translate the code before it is executed."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Maximum 1 mark.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"To convert it to binary/machine code // The processor can only understand machine code","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2.5.1-8b","parent_question":8,"topic":"translators (compilers vs interpreters)","marks":4,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Either a compiler or an interpreter can translate the code.\\n\\nDescribe two differences between how a compiler and an interpreter would translate the code."},{"type":"text","value":"Difference 1: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"Difference 2: ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark to be awarded for the correct identification and one for a valid description up to a maximum of 4 marks. No more than 2 marks for answers relating only to interpreters and no more than 2 marks for answers only relating to compilers.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Compiler translates all the code in one go","marks":1},{"criteria":"Whereas an interpreter translates one line at a time","marks":1},{"criteria":"Compiler creates an executable","marks":1},{"criteria":"Whereas an interpreter does not / executes one line at a time","marks":1},{"criteria":"Compiler reports errors at the end","marks":1},{"criteria":"Whereas an interpreter stops when it finds an error","marks":1}]}}]'),RT={paper_id:gV,qualification:fV,component:yV,title:bV,year:wV,session:vV,total_marks:AV,questions:kV},xV="J277-TOPIC-2.5.2",_V="J277",qV="TOPIC",CV="The Integrated Development Environment (IDE)",SV=null,TV=null,MV=17,jV=[{question_id:"2.5.2-1",parent_question:1,topic:"IDE tools",marks:4,command_word:"identify and describe",content:[{type:"text",value:"This flowchart uses iteration."},{type:"image",kind:"diagram",src:"data/png/j277/diagrams/iteration-flowchart.png",alt_text:"Iteration flowchart that repeatedly outputs OK and subtracts 2 from x until x is less than 0."},{type:"text",value:"A programmer implements the flowchart as a program in a high-level language using an Integrated Development Environment (IDE)."},{type:"text",value:"Identify and describe two tools that the programmer could use in the IDE to create a program from the flowchart."},{type:"text",value:"Tool 1: ____"},{type:"text",value:"Description: ____"},{type:"text",value:"Tool 2: ____"},{type:"text",value:"Description: ____"}],answer:{guidance:[{type:"text",value:"1 mark for tool and 1 mark for a matching description (max 4 marks, i.e. two tool/description pairs)."},{type:"list",items:["Description must add more than is given in the identification of the feature.","If compiler and interpreter are given as two distinct features, allow both with suitable descriptions, but do not allow translator alongside compiler/interpreter.","Description must match the tool — if the tool name is wrong or missing, do not give the description mark.","Allow sensible references to AI where appropriate.","Allow other sensible features (line numbering, auto indent, collapsed blocks, etc) with suitable description.","Do not allow features of programming languages (comments, casting, etc)."]},{type:"text",value:"Example acceptable answers (tool — description):"},{type:"list",items:["Text/code editor — allows program code to be written/entered/changed or allows errors to be fixed.","Debugger / error reporting / diagnostics — identifies/finds/checks for errors, shows location/detail of errors, suggests fixes.","Run-time environment / output window — allows program/code to be run/executed, shows output of the program.","Translator / compiler / interpreter — convert to low-level/machine code; allow program to be executed; produce executable file (compiler only); stops execution when error found (interpreter only).","Stepping — execute/run the program line by line.","Variable watch — see the contents/data held in variables or how variables change.","Break points — allow the program to stop at a chosen position.","Pretty printing / keyword highlighting — allows keywords/variables to be coloured/identified.","Keyword completion / autocomplete / autocorrect / syntax suggestion — suggests/corrects code/syntax.","GUI builder — allows creation of user interface / buttons by example."]}],marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Tool 1 correctly identified (e.g. editor, debugger, run-time environment, translator, stepping, variable watch, break points, keyword highlighting, autocomplete, GUI builder)",marks:1},{criteria:"Matching description of Tool 1 that adds more than the tool name",marks:1},{criteria:"Tool 2 correctly identified (a different tool from Tool 1)",marks:1},{criteria:"Matching description of Tool 2 that adds more than the tool name",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2.5.2-2a",parent_question:2,topic:"high-level languages and translators",marks:4,command_word:"describe",content:[{type:"text",value:"A programmer is creating a computer game. Explain two advantages of using a high-level language to create the computer game."}],answer:{guidance:[{type:"text",value:"Mark in pairs: 1 mark for an advantage and 1 mark for an expansion/description, up to 4 marks total. Accept other reasonable advantages and descriptions."},{type:"text",value:"Example acceptable answers (advantage — expansion):"},{type:"list",items:["Easier / quicker to create — language closer to English / uses keywords.","Provides higher level of abstraction from the underlying processor — don't usually have to deal with allocating memory.","Portable / processor independent — can write once for many processor types (e.g. mobile)."]}],marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Advantage 1 identified (e.g. easier/quicker to create; higher level of abstraction; portable/processor independent)",marks:1},{criteria:"Expansion of Advantage 1 (e.g. closer to English; no need to allocate memory; write once for many processors)",marks:1},{criteria:"Advantage 2 identified (different from Advantage 1)",marks:1},{criteria:"Expansion of Advantage 2",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2.5.2-2b",parent_question:2,topic:"translators (compiler and interpreter)",marks:3,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"The IDE includes a translator, such as a compiler or an interpreter."},{type:"text",value:"Tick (✓) one box in each row to identify whether each statement describes the use of a compiler, an interpreter, or both."},{type:"table",headers:["Statement","Compiler","Interpreter","Both"],rows:[["Translates high-level code to low-level instructions.","","",""],["Produces an executable file.","","",""],["Program needs to be translated every time it is run.","","",""]]}],answer:{guidance:[{type:"text",value:"1 mark per row for the correct tick."},{type:"list",items:["Translates high-level code to low-level instructions — Both.","Produces an executable file — Compiler.","Program needs to be translated every time it is run — Interpreter."]}],marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Translates high-level code to low-level instructions = Both",marks:1},{criteria:"Produces an executable file = Compiler",marks:1},{criteria:"Program needs to be translated every time it is run = Interpreter",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2.5.2-3",parent_question:3,topic:"IDE tools",marks:4,command_word:"describe",content:[{type:"text",value:"A translator is a common tool found in an Integrated Development Environment (IDE)."},{type:"text",value:"Describe two other common tools or facilities that an IDE can provide."}],answer:{guidance:[{type:"text",value:"1 mark per bullet, max 4 marks. Mark in pairs: 1 mark for tool and 1 mark for description. Allow other tools available in an IDE with suitable expansion (e.g. breakpoints, watch window, stepping, pretty printing, etc)."},{type:"text",value:"Example acceptable answers (tool — description):"},{type:"list",items:["Editor — to enable program code to be entered/edited.","Error diagnostics / debugger — to display information about errors / location of errors / suggest solutions.","Run-time environment — to enable program to be run / check for runtime errors / test the program."]}],marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Tool 1 identified (e.g. editor, error diagnostics/debugger, run-time environment, breakpoints, watch window, stepping, pretty printing)",marks:1},{criteria:"Description of Tool 1 (expansion of purpose)",marks:1},{criteria:"Tool 2 identified (different from Tool 1)",marks:1},{criteria:"Description of Tool 2 (expansion of purpose)",marks:1}]}},{question_id:"2.5.2-4",parent_question:4,topic:"IDE features",marks:2,command_word:"identify",content:[{type:"text",value:"The area of a circle is calculated using the formula π × r² where π is equal to 3.142 and r is the radius."},{type:"text",value:"A program is written to allow a user to enter the radius of a circle as a whole number between 1 and 30, then calculate and output the area of the circle."},{type:"code",language:"pseudocode",value:`01  radius = 0
