- environmental issues
- benefits and drawbacks`}],answer:{guidance:"Banded mark scheme. Top-band responses include developed benefits and drawbacks, at least one ethical issue and one environmental issue, and clear reference to both the company and the customers. Indicative content includes increased profit or sales for the company, lower purchase cost for some customers, possible damage to reputation, customers being forced to replace devices more often, more e-waste, recycling or reuse of old devices, fairness to customers, and whether customers are clearly told about the decision.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Band 1 (1-2 marks): Basic point about benefit, drawback, ethical, or environmental impact with limited development",marks:2},{criteria:"Band 2 (3-5 marks): Reasonable discussion covering some required areas with some linked explanation",marks:3},{criteria:"Band 3 (6-8 marks): Balanced, developed discussion covering benefits and drawbacks with ethical and environmental issues, linked to both company and customers",marks:3}]}},{question_id:"1.6-Essay-Questions-2",parent_question:2,topic:"open source vs proprietary",marks:8,command_word:"discuss",content:[{type:"text",value:"A computer programmer has developed a computer game that they want to release for users to download over the internet."},{type:"text",value:"The programmer needs to decide whether to release the game as open source or proprietary software."},{type:"text",value:"Discuss the features, benefits and drawbacks of each type of licence for this program and make a recommendation to the programmer."},{type:"text",value:`- features of each licence
- legal and ethical issues of each licence
- benefits and drawbacks of each licence`}],answer:{guidance:"Banded mark scheme. Top-band responses cover both open source and proprietary software, address legal and ethical issues, benefits and drawbacks, and give a justified recommendation. Indicative content includes open source usually being free with editable source code and redistribution rights, proprietary software being sold with restricted access to the code, copyright applying to both, wider access and easier bug fixing for open source, limited financial gain for open source, and greater profit and control for proprietary software.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Band 1 (1-2 marks): Basic facts about open source and/or proprietary software",marks:2},{criteria:"Band 2 (3-5 marks): Reasonable discussion covering some required features, issues, benefits, or drawbacks",marks:3},{criteria:"Band 3 (6-8 marks): Developed comparison of both licence types with justified recommendation",marks:3}]}},{question_id:"1.6-Essay-Questions-3",parent_question:3,topic:"facial recognition impact",marks:8,command_word:"discuss",content:[{type:"text",value:"A shopping centre has a security system that includes CCTV cameras to record activities in the centre."},{type:"text",value:"The security system is being upgraded to include the use of facial recognition to identify, track the movements of and record individuals throughout the shopping centre."},{type:"text",value:"Discuss the positive and negative impacts of this upgrade including:"},{type:"text",value:`- ethical issues
- privacy issues
- legal issues`}],answer:{guidance:"Banded mark scheme. Indicative content includes legal requirements under the Data Protection Act, informing customers, keeping data secure, using evidence to identify criminals, customers feeling safer, people feeling watched or tracked, privacy concerns about storing movement data, and the fact that the centre is private property. Stronger answers give a balanced discussion across legal, ethical, and privacy issues.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Band 1 (1-2 marks): Basic point about one impact with limited development",marks:2},{criteria:"Band 2 (3-5 marks): Reasonable discussion of most required areas with some explanation",marks:3},{criteria:"Band 3 (6-8 marks): Balanced, developed discussion across legal, ethical, and privacy issues",marks:3}]}},{question_id:"1.6-Essay-Questions-4",parent_question:4,topic:"AI and social networking",marks:8,command_word:"discuss",content:[{type:"text",value:"*Social networking websites use artificial intelligence (AI) to monitor posts from users."},{type:"text",value:"Discuss the positive and negative uses of AI by social networking websites including:"},{type:"text",value:`- legal issues
- ethical issues
- privacy issues`}],answer:{guidance:"Banded mark scheme. Indicative content includes checking posts for plagiarism or illegal material, complying with data-protection rules, users agreeing through terms and conditions, concerns about users being monitored or posts being blocked incorrectly, safer use of the website, and privacy concerns about users feeling watched. Stronger answers balance positives and negatives across legal, ethical, and privacy issues.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Band 1 (1-2 marks): Basic point about one issue with limited development",marks:2},{criteria:"Band 2 (3-5 marks): Reasonable discussion of most required areas with some explanation",marks:3},{criteria:"Band 3 (6-8 marks): Balanced, developed discussion across legal, ethical, and privacy issues",marks:3}]}},{question_id:"1.6-Essay-Questions-5",parent_question:5,topic:"digital technology in medicine",marks:8,command_word:"discuss",content:[{type:"text",value:"The use of digital technology in medicine is constantly evolving."},{type:"text",value:"Discuss the impact of digital technology on medicine including:"},{type:"text",value:`- diagnosing patients
- treating patients
- storage of records`}],answer:{guidance:"Banded mark scheme. Indicative content includes diagnosis becoming faster through searching records, pattern finding, or AI-assisted equipment; treatment using automation or remote specialist control; and centralised storage of records being easier for medical staff to access. Drawbacks include incorrect diagnoses, hacking, fatal software errors, reduced human interaction, and privacy or security risks if centralised records are leaked.",marks_breakdown:[{criteria:"Band 1 (1-2 marks): Basic point about diagnosis, treatment, or record storage",marks:2},{criteria:"Band 2 (3-5 marks): Reasonable discussion covering some of the required areas with linked explanation",marks:3},{criteria:"Band 3 (6-8 marks): Developed discussion across diagnosis, treatment, and record storage with balanced impacts",marks:3}]}},{question_id:"1.6-Essay-Questions-6",parent_question:6,topic:"smartphone upgrade impact",marks:8,command_word:"discuss",content:[{type:"text",value:"* People often want to buy the most up-to-date smartphones, even though the smartphone they own still works."},{type:"text",value:"Discuss the impact of people wanting to upgrade to the latest smartphone."},{type:"text",value:`In your answer, you might consider the impact on:
