r monitors/manages/configures the system)","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-005.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-018.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-2-b-i.png"}},{"question_id":"2(b)(ii)","parent_question":2,"topic":"encryption software","marks":3,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Explain the purpose and function of encryption software."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark each to max 3. Valid points include:"},{"type":"list","items":["jumbles / mixes up / encodes / scrambles / cyphers the data","encrypts / decrypts using an algorithm and/or key","makes the data meaningless if intercepted or accessed without authorisation — it cannot be understood or used"]},{"type":"text","value":"For MP3 do not accept 'it cannot be read' or 'it cannot be accessed' — encryption does not stop interception or opening of the file, only understanding of its contents."}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Scrambles / jumbles / encodes / cyphers the data","marks":1},{"criteria":"Encrypts and/or decrypts using an algorithm and/or a key","marks":1},{"criteria":"Makes the data meaningless / unintelligible if intercepted or accessed without authorisation (not 'cannot be read' or 'cannot be accessed')","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-005.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-018.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-2-b-ii.png"}},{"question_id":"3","parent_question":3,"topic":"technology impact discussion","marks":8,"command_word":"discuss","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A company designs and builds tablet computers. The company wants to reduce the cost of manufacturing their tablet computers. The company also decides to stop releasing software updates for their older tablet computers. This means customers will need to change their devices more often."},{"type":"text","value":"Discuss the impact of these decisions on the company and the customers."},{"type":"text","value":"Include in your answer:"},{"type":"text","value":"- ethical issues"},{"type":"text","value":"- environmental issues"},{"type":"text","value":"- benefits and drawbacks."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Levels-of-response marking out of 8."},{"type":"table","headers":["Level","Marks","Guidance"],"rows":[["Level 3","6-8 marks","thorough knowledge applied directly and consistently to the context; weighs both sides; covers benefits AND drawbacks, at least one ethical AND at least one environmental issue, and references both customer and company with expanded points for top of band"],["Level 2","3-5 marks","reasonable knowledge, generally accurate but at times underdeveloped; covers benefits or drawbacks (both needed for top of band); covers ethical and/or environmental; some points expanded; may only reference customer or company"],["Level 1","1-2 marks","basic knowledge with limited understanding; unsupported assertions; covers at least one of ethical/environmental/benefit/drawback; may not reference customer or company"],["0 marks","","no attempt or response not worthy of credit"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Indicative content — Ethical issues:"},{"type":"list","items":["will cost to customer remain the same (unfair to customers)","will customers be informed (deceit)","profit can be reinvested or paid to staff","ethical to the company but unethical to customers","reduced cost may damage reputation long-term","customers wanting up-to-date devices are prepared to spend regularly","lower purchase cost may make devices accessible to more people"]},{"type":"text","value":"Environmental issues:"},{"type":"list","items":["increase in e-waste from disposed products","older devices could be redistributed to people without devices","products could be recycled for components"]},{"type":"text","value":"Benefits and drawbacks — Company:"},{"type":"list","items":["increased sales","increased profit","potential decrease in popularity/reputation"]},{"type":"text","value":"Customer:"},{"type":"list","items":["increase in overall cost of ownership","ability to buy when previously unaffordable if the initial cost is lower","less reliable devices","effort/time to install and set up new devices more regularly"]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Level 3 top of band (8 marks): thorough discussion covering benefits and drawbacks, at least one ethical and at least one environmental issue, referencing both customer and company with expanded, substantiated points","marks":8}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-002.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-019.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-3.png"}},{"question_id":"4(a)","parent_question":4,"topic":"LAN vs WAN","marks":2,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A youth centre is creating a network with 20 computers in a single building that will be connected in a Local Area Network (LAN)."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify two reasons why this network will be a LAN and not a Wide Area Network (WAN)."},{"type":"text","value":"1: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"2: ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark each to max 2. Award any two correct points as long as they are not contradicted. Valid points:"},{"type":"list","items":["small geographical location / single building","no use of external infrastructure / all hardware is owned or managed by the youth centre","dedicated hardware that is not shared with anyone else or another business","it is not connecting networks together (as a WAN does)"]},{"type":"text","value":"Note: a LAN and WAN are not defined by the number of computers connected — distance and hardware ownership are the distinguishing factors."}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"First valid reason (e.g. small geographical area / single building, or hardware is owned and managed by the youth centre, or no external infrastructure used)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Second valid reason (e.g. dedicated hardware not shared with other businesses, or it is not connecting separate networks together as a WAN does)","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-006.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-022.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-4-a.png"}},{"question_id":"4(b)(i)","parent_question":4,"topic":"mesh topology definition","marks":2,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The network design connects the computers in a mesh topology."},{"type":"text","value":"Describe what is meant by a mesh topology."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark each to max 2. Valid points:"},{"type":"list","items":["(partial mesh) all devices are connected to one or more other devices, OR (full mesh) all devices are connected to every other device","no need for central management / switch / device / node (all devices are equal / decentralised)","multiple routes or paths between devices"]},{"type":"text","value":"For MP1 accept by benefit of the doubt 'each device is connected to other devices' or 'all devices are connected'."},{"type":"text","value":"For MP2 do not accept 'no central server' on its own."}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Describes that devices are connected to one or more / every other device","marks":1},{"criteria":"Describes a second feature: no central switch/node (decentralised / all devices equal), OR multiple routes/paths exist between devices","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-007.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-024.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-4-b-i.png"}},{"question_id":"4(b)(ii)","parent_question":4,"topic":"mesh vs star topology","marks":4,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Describe one benefit and one drawback of the network using a mesh topology instead of a star topology."},{"type":"text","value":"Benefit: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"Drawback: ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark for a point and 1 mark for an expansion/reason; max 2 marks for the benefit and max 2 marks for the drawback."},{"type":"text","value":"Any of the points can be the benefit/drawback with a matching expansion."},{"type":"text","value":"Do not accept 'faster/slower transmission speeds' — these depend on media and many other factors."},{"type":"text","value":"Benefit points and expansions:"},{"type":"list","items":["no purchase/cost of a central switch or device (lower cost to install/maintain; no need to set up a central device)","more connections/paths between devices or alternate routes (no single point of failure; if a connection breaks the nodes can still connect via another route; more robust structure)","more scalable / can support more devices or nodes (easier to add devices; can add or remove nodes without impacting others)","decrease in latency (fewer collisions)","can be set up over a larger area or provide a more stable connection (each device can act as a repeater)"]},{"type":"text","value":"Drawback points and expansions:"},{"type":"list","items":["large number of / more connections or wires (can involve redundant connections; this is impractical)","reduced central management / control / oversight (less control over transfer or security)","less secure by example (more routes/points/devices for data interception, attack or unauthorised access)","difficult to find an error (because of the multiple routes where the error could occur)","mesh uses more power (more nodes involved in each transmission)"]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Benefit point (e.g. no single point of failure, no central switch required, more scalable)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Expansion of the benefit (e.g. if one connection breaks data can still route through another path; easier to add devices without disrupting others)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Drawback point (e.g. large number of cables/connections, less secure, difficult to locate errors, uses more power)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Expansion of the drawback (e.g. can involve redundant connections that are impractical to install; more routes means more points of interception; errors could occur on any of many routes)","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-007.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-023.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-4-b-ii.png"}},{"question_id":"4(c)(i)","parent_question":4,"topic":"Wi-Fi connection benefits","marks":3,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The network design originally only had wired connections. The design is updated to include wireless connections via Wi-Fi."},{"type":"text","value":"Explain the benefits to the youth centre of also providing Wi-Fi connections."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark each to max 3."},{"type":"list","items":["MP1: easier to add more devices/users to the network.","MP2: can have more devices/connections/users (more scalable) — without the cost of purchasing or installing additional wired connections.","Devices are not fixed to one spot / can be moved / can connect from anywhere in wireless range — allowing people to use them where they are needed or where there is no physical connection.","Reduces risk of additional trailing wires (less potential damage to equipment or wires).","Connects a wider range or more types of device (e.g. mobile phones, tablets) that do not have ports / only have wireless connections.","Provides a backup network if the wired network fails.","Due to each node acting as a repeater (in a mesh) the network will have a greater range."]},{"type":"text","value":"'More devices can be added easily' on its own is MP1 only."}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Benefit 1: devices are portable / can be moved / can connect from anywhere in range, allowing use where needed","marks":1},{"criteria":"Benefit 2: easier or cheaper to add more devices/users because no additional wired connections need to be purchased or installed (more scalable)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Benefit 3: connects a wider range of devices such as phones and tablets that have no ports / reduces trailing wires / provides a backup if the wired network fails","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-008.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-024.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-4-c-i.png"}},{"question_id":"4(c)(ii)","parent_question":4,"topic":"network performance factors","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The decision to use wired and/or wireless connections can affect the performance of the network."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the table by explaining how each factor can affect the performance of a network."},{"type":"table","headers":["Factor","How it affects performance"],"rows":[["Bandwidth",""],["Number of users accessing the network at the same time",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark per bullet to max 2 for each factor. Allow the reverse of each point."},{"type":"text","value":"Do not award references to internet speed alone. Points need to reference more/less data in the correct context."},{"type":"text","value":"Bandwidth:"},{"type":"list","items":["more bandwidth = faster network/transmission (BOD better performance) because more data is transferred simultaneously or per second","less bandwidth = slower network/worse performance because less data can be transferred per second"]},{"type":"text","value":"Number of users:"},{"type":"list","items":["more users = slower network/transmission (BOD worse performance) because more data is being transferred simultaneously / more traffic / bandwidth is shared between users / more congestion or collisions","fewer users = faster network / better performance because more bandwidth is available per user"]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Bandwidth — states the direction of change (higher or lower bandwidth) and links it to faster/slower transmission or better/worse performance","marks":1},{"criteria":"Bandwidth — expansion explaining why (e.g. because more/less data is transferred per second or simultaneously)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Number of users — more users results in slower network / worse performance","marks":1},{"criteria":"Number of users — expansion explaining why (e.g. bandwidth is shared between users / more congestion / more collisions / more traffic simultaneously)","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-008.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-023.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-4-c-ii.png"}},{"question_id":"4(d)","parent_question":4,"topic":"cloud storage drawbacks","marks":5,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The youth centre is going to store data about users and events using cloud storage."},{"type":"text","value":"Describe the drawbacks to the youth centre of storing the data on the cloud."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark each to max 5. MP1 needs more than 'high cost' — it needs identification of ongoing or hosting costs etc. MP3 just 'poor/low security' is not enough (NE)."},{"type":"text","value":"Accept 'data may be sold' as an example of misuse. Valid points:"},{"type":"list","items":["can be expensive for large amounts of data / long term / hosting (may be an ongoing subscription; no control over changing costs)","may be a limited amount of storage","no control over security (need to rely on the provider for security)","may be hacked / stolen / intercepted / affected by a virus","may lose (personal) data or lose access to data","may go against DPA/legislation / data may be misused by the provider","may not be clear where in the world the data is stored","limited or no control over access","cloud company could go down","no control over backup / may not have automatic backups (data not retrievable)","need internet access — no internet means no data (access speed depends on network or connection speed)","concerns over ownership of the data","need to remember login details (may forget or lose them)","users may need training"]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Drawback 1: ongoing cost (e.g. subscription for hosting, or no control over changing costs)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Drawback 2: need internet access to reach the data / access speed depends on connection (no internet = no data)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Drawback 3: no control over security — must rely on the provider; data may be hacked / stolen / intercepted","marks":1},{"criteria":"Drawback 4: limited or no control over where data is stored, who can access it, or how it is backed up (may not have automatic backups)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Drawback 5: risk of losing data or access if the cloud provider goes down, or risk of data misuse (e.g. provider selling data) which may breach DPA","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-009.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-026.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-4-d.png"}},{"question_id":"4(e)(i)","parent_question":4,"topic":"internet connection device","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Users will have access to the internet."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify one device that will be required to allow the LAN to connect to the internet."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for router or modem. Do not accept network interface card, wires or 'a computer'.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Router or modem identified","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27701_Computer_systems_June_2025 (1).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/question/page-010.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/markscheme/page-024.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-1-2025-june/dev-qa/q-4-e-i.png"}},{"question_id":"4(e)(ii)","parent_question":4,"topic":"IPv4 address validation","marks":4,"command_word":"tick","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The computers will be allocated an IPv4 address."},{"type":"text","value":"Tick one box on each row to identify if the IPv4 address is valid or invalid."},{"type":"table","headers":["IPv4 address","Valid","Invalid"],"rows":[["192.154.21.2","",""],["258.0.0.3","",""],["56.1.2.66.1","",""],["251.58.3.7","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark for 