s a discount card"],["C","The current day is Saturday"]]},{"type":"text","value":"The logic system P = (A OR B) AND NOT C is used."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the following logic diagram for P = (A OR B) AND NOT C by drawing one logic gate in each box."},{"type":"image","kind":"diagram","src":"j277/yearpapers/paper2-2022/2a_unannotated.png","alt_text":"Unannotated logic diagram for P = (A OR B) AND NOT C"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark per correctly drawn gate, with correct symbols used. The three gates required are:"},{"type":"list","items":["an OR gate taking inputs A and B (A OR B)","a NOT gate applied to input C (NOT C)","an AND gate combining the two intermediate results to produce P"]},{"type":"text","value":"The NOT gate must include the circle for inversion; the OR and AND gates must not have a circle. Mark the shape of each gate, not any name written next to it. Lines do not have to be drawn or joined up, but if they are, gates must have the correct number of inputs/outputs - penalise once then follow through."}],"image":{"kind":"diagram","src":"j277/yearpapers/paper2-2022/2a-answer.png","alt_text":"Completed logic diagram showing green OR, NOT and AND gates over the original question","caption":"Model answer for 2(a)(i)"},"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"OR gate correctly drawn for A OR B","marks":1},{"criteria":"NOT gate correctly drawn (with inversion circle) for NOT C","marks":1},{"criteria":"AND gate correctly drawn combining the two intermediate outputs to produce P","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_June_2022 (3).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2022-june/question/page-003.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2022-june/markscheme/page-024.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2022-june/dev-qa/q-2-a-i.png"}},{"question_id":"2(a)(ii)","parent_question":2,"topic":"truth table purpose