ice = 60 * nights\\n  elseif room == \\"premium\\" then\\n    price = 80 * nights\\n  endif\\n  return price\\nendfunction"}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Defines a new function with a function / def header named newPrice","marks":1},{"criteria":"Takes at least two parameters (nights and room)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correctly calculates the price using the parameters (60 * nights for basic, 80 * nights for premium)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns the calculated price from the function","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_June_2022 (3).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2022-june/question/page-016.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2022-june/markscheme/page-042.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2022-june/dev-qa/q-5-c-i.png"}},{"question_id":"5(c)(ii)","parent_question":5,"topic":"function call code","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write program code, that uses `newPrice()`, to output the price of staying in a Premium room for 5 nights."},{"type":"text","value":"You must use either:\\n- OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n- a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark each, to max 3."},{"type":"list","items":["call the function newPrice","pass (\\"premium\\", 5) as parameters - order of parameters is not important; \\"premium\\" must use string delimiters (quotes)","output the returned value"]},{"type":"text","value":"Do not allow function definitions for BP1. Ignore capitalisation of newPrice. The candidate can store the returned value in a variable and then print, or store parameters in variables before passing - both acceptable. Ignore superfluous code. Do not credit answers where newPrice is overwritten prior to use. Allow call if brackets are missing"},{"type":"code","value":"print(newPrice(\\"premium\\", 5))\\nor\