:1},{"criteria":"Third valid benefit of using a compiler","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_June_2024 (3).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2024-june/question/page-007.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2024-june/markscheme/page-024.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2024-june/dev-qa/q-7-b.png"}},{"question_id":"8(a)","parent_question":8,"topic":"maintainability improvements","marks":4,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"An algorithm stores the `position` of a character on a straight line as an integer. A user can move the character left or right."},{"type":"text","value":"The following algorithm:\\n• generates one random number between 1 and 512 (inclusive) to store as the `position`\\n• prompts the user to input a `direction` to move (left or right)\\n• takes a `direction` as input until a valid `direction` is input."},{"type":"code","language":"ocr-reference","value":"p = random(1, 512)\\nprint(\\"The position is \\", p)\\na = \\"\\"\\nwhile a != \\"left\\" and a != \\"right\\"\\n    a = input(\\"Enter direction, left or right\\")\\nendwhile"},{"type":"text","value":"Describe **two** ways to improve the maintainability of the algorithm."},{"type":"text","value":"1  ____________________________________________________________"},{"type":"text","value":"2  ____________________________________________________________"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"2 marks max per group (one method + expansion / example applied to this algorithm)."},{"type":"text","value":"Valid groups (method — explanation — example):"},{"type":"list","items":["**Meaningful identifiers / variable names** — describes / shows what they store / purpose of variable — example: `position` instead of `p`, `direction` instead of `a`","**Comments** — make it easier for other programmers to follow / understand the code / easier to debug — example: a suitable comment for this algorithm","**Use of subroutines** — reuse blocks of code / make code easier to follow — example: a subroutine for this algorithm","**Use of constants** — store data that will not change during program execution / so data can be changed in one place only — example: store 512 as a constant"]},{"type":"text","value":"Benefit of doubt for notes / whitespace / blank lines as alternatives to comments."},{"type":"text","value":"Do not allow:"},{"type":"list","items":["Indentation (already done in the program given)","\\"Makes it easier to understand\\" by itself (too vague)","Expansions where it isn\'t clear which method is being discussed"]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"First maintainability method identified (e.g. meaningful identifiers, comments, subroutines, constants)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Expansion / example of the first method applied to this algorithm","marks":1},{"criteria":"Second maintainability method identified","marks":1},{"criteria":"Expansion / example of the second method applied to this algorithm","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_June_2024 (3).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2024-june/question/page-008.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2024-june/markscheme/page-025.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2024-june/dev-qa/q-8-a.png"}},{"question_id":"8(b)","parent_question":8,"topic":"moveCharacter function","marks":6,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"If the character moves left, 5 is subtracted from the `position`. If the character moves right, 5 is added to the `position`. The `position` of the character can only be between 1 and 512 inclusive."},{"type":"text","value":"The function `moveCharacter()`:\\n• takes the `direction` (left or right) and current `position` as parameters\\n• changes `position` based on `direction`\\n• sets `position` to 1 if the new `position` is less than 1\\n• sets `position` to 512 if the new `position` is greater than 512\\n• returns the new `position`."},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the function `moveCharacter()`"},{"type":"code","language":"ocr-reference","value":"function moveCharacter(direction, position)\\n\\n\\nendfunction"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark each to max 6."},{"type":"list","items":["**BP1:** Appropriate use of both parameters and no additional inputs / incorrect overwrites that affect the outcome of the algorithm","**BP2:** Attempt at selection","**BP3:** Correctly checking if `direction` is \\"left\\" and subtracting 5 from `position` (or equivalent)","**BP4:** Correctly checking if `direction` is \\"right\\" and adding 5 to `position` (or equivalent)","**BP5:** Ensuring `position` is between 1 and 512 inclusive","**BP6:** Returning the updated `position`"]},{"type":"text","value":"Example solution:"},{"type":"code","value":"if direction == \\"left\\" then\\n    position = position - 5\\nelseif direction == \\"right\\" then\\n    position = position + 5\\nendif\\nif position < 1 then\\n    position = 1\\nelseif position > 512 then\\n    position = 512\\nendif\\nreturn position"},{"type":"text","value":"Acceptable variations:"},{"type":"list","items":["Allow `else` for BP3/BP4","Allow `<=`, `>=` and equivalents for BP5","Accept flowchart / structured English (must not just repeat the question)"]},{"type":"text","value":"Constraints:"},{"type":"list","items":["Do not award BP5 if it comes before BP3/BP4 (otherwise will alter `position` value)","BP6 only awarded if an attempt is made at calculating new `position`","For minor syntax errors (e.g. missing quotation marks, `==` for assignment, spaces in variable names) penalise once then follow-through"]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Appropriate use of both parameters with no additional inputs / incorrect overwrites","marks":1},{"criteria":"Attempt at selection (