el = 2\\nelseif code == \\"UTV\\" then\\n  level = 3\\nelse\\n  level = 1\\nendif"}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Inputs a code from the user and stores or uses it","marks":1},{"criteria":"Repeats input until the code is exactly three characters long","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks for SVA","marks":1},{"criteria":"Sets level to 2 for SVA","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks for UTV and sets level to 3","marks":1},{"criteria":"Sets level to 1 for any other valid three-character code","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2023 (2).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/question/page-009.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/markscheme/page-024.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/dev-qa/q-6-e-i.png"}},{"question_id":"6(e)(ii)","parent_question":6,"topic":"next level function","marks":3,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"When a player completes a level, they move to the next level. Once level 3 is completed, the game starts again at level 1."},{"type":"text","value":"Write a function called `nextlevel()` that:\\n- takes the current level as a parameter\\n- works out the integer value of the next level the player moves to\\n- returns the integer value."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"1 mark per bullet point. Accept correct use of MOD for calculating the wrap from level 3 to level 1. Allow follow-through if the value is output/calculated but not returned."},{"type":"code","language":"ocr","value":"function nextlevel(oldlevel)\\n  if oldlevel == 3 then\\n    return 1\\n  else\\n    return oldlevel + 1\\n  endif\\nendfunction"}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Defines function nextlevel() with at least one parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns parameter plus 1 for levels before 3","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns 1 when the parameter is 3","marks":1}]