ce/dev-qa/q-7-c.png"}},{"question_id":"7(d)(i)","parent_question":7,"topic":"pay calculation algorithm","marks":4,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Pilots are paid a set amount each day. Pilots also get an additional payment for each mile they have flown that day. These payments are shown in the table."},{"type":"table","headers":["Flying experience","Pay per day","Pay per mile"],"rows":[["Fewer than 2 years","£120.00","£0.45"],["2 years to 5 years inclusive","£150.00","£0.65"],["More than 5 years","£180.00","£0.85"]]},{"type":"text","value":"For example, a pilot with 3 years\' experience who flies 100 miles in one day will receive £215.00 pay:\\n- £150.00 pay for the day\\n- £65.00 additional payment (£0.65 pay per mile x 100 miles)\\n- Add £150.00 and £65.00 together to get £215.00 total pay"},{"type":"text","value":"Complete the algorithm to:\\n- Calculate the total pay for the pilot for that day\\n\\nYou must use either:\\n- OCR Exam Reference Language, or\\n- A high-level programming language that you have studied."},{"type":"code","language":"ocr","value":"experience = input(\\"Enter years of experience\\")\\nmiles = input(\\"Enter miles flown\\")\\ntotalPay = 0"}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"Award marks for selection and correct calculations in each band. Follow through for the final band only where a reasonable attempt at calculating pay has been made."},{"type":"code","language":"ocr","value":"if experience < 2 then\\n  totalPay = 120 + (0.45 * miles)\\nelseif experience <= 5 then\\n  totalPay = 150 + (0.65 * miles)\\nelse\\n  totalPay = 180 + (0.85 * miles)\\nendif"}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Attempts to use selection","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for fewer than 2 years\' experience","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for 2 to 5 years inclusive","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates pay correctly for more than 5 years\' experience","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2023 (2).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/question/page-015.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/markscheme/page-026.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/dev-qa/q-7-d-i.png"}},{"question_id":"7(d)(ii)","parent_question":7,"topic":"function refactoring","marks":2,"command_word":"refine","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The programmer decides to make a function to calculate the total pay for the pilot.\\n\\nThe function is called `calculatePay()`.\\n\\nThe function takes the values for experience and miles as two parameters and returns the total pay for the pilot."},{"type":"text","value":"Refine the algorithm to use this function and output the pay for the pilot."},{"type":"code","language":"ocr","value":"experience = input(\\"Enter years of experience\\")\\nmiles = input(\\"Enter miles flown\\")\\n____ = calculatePay( ____ , ____ )\\nprint(totalPay)"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Correct completion: `totalPay = calculatePay(experience, miles)`. Accept the parameters in either order where logically valid.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Assigns the function return value to totalPay","marks":1},{"criteria":"Passes experience and miles as parameters to calculatePay()","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2023 (2).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/question/page-011.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/markscheme/page-026.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/dev-qa/q-7-d-ii.png"}},{"question_id":"7(e)","parent_question":7,"topic":"file write algorithm","marks":4,"command_word":"design","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A text file is used to store pilot codes and dates of birth.\\n\\n\\nThe text file is named `pilots.txt`. The contents of some of this file are shown:"},{"type":"code","value":"JP670,17/05/1986\\nCC200,31/06/1980\\nSM720,01/04/1976\\nGC730,06/06/1978"},{"type":"text","value":"Design an algorithm to:\\n- ask the user to input a pilot code and a date of birth\\n- write these inputs to the `pilots.txt` text file."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"One mark per bullet point. Award the file-close mark for implicit closing, for example Python `with`. Allow data to be written either as both values or as one concatenated string separated by a comma."},{"type":"list","items":["Ask the user for two inputs and store/use them","Open `pilots.txt` for write or append","Write both inputs to the opened text file","Close the text file"]}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Asks for and stores/uses pilot code and date of birth","marks":1},{"criteria":"Opens pilots.txt for write or append","marks":1},{"criteria":"Writes both inputs to the file","marks":1},{"criteria":"Closes the file or uses an implicit close","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2023 (2).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/question/page-017.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/markscheme/page-025.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/dev-qa/q-7-e.png"}},{"question_id":"7(f)","parent_question":7,"topic":"2D array pilot validation","marks":6,"command_word":"create","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A pilot is allowed to fly a maximum of 9 hours per day. The pilot code and the hours flown for each flight in one day are stored in a 2D array of strings with the identifier `journeys`.\\n\\nThe data in `journeys` is shown."},{"type":"table","headers":["Index","[0]","[1]"],"rows":[["[0]","\\"SM720\\"","\\"4.5\\""],["[1]","\\"GC730\\"","\\"3\\""],["[2]","\\"JP670\\"","\\"2\\""],["[3]","\\"GC730\\"","\\"3.5\\""],["[4]","\\"CC200\\"","\\"9\\""],["[5]","\\"RY320\\"","\\"12\\""]]},{"type":"text","value":"The value of `journeys[3,1]` is `\\"3.5\\"`."},{"type":"text","value":"Create a function, `pilotValid()`, that:\\n- takes a pilot code as a parameter\\n- uses the 2D array `journeys` to calculate the number of hours that the pilot has flown\\n- returns `valid` if the pilot has flown 9 hours or fewer or `warning` if the pilot has flown for more than 9 hours\\n- uses casting where needed.\\n\\nYou must use either OCR Exam Reference Language or a high-level programming language that you have studied."}],"answer":{"guidance":[{"type":"text","value":"One mark per bullet point to max 6. Do not allow casting to integer where decimal journeys are present. Allow follow-through for the check and return marks if a reasonable calculation attempt has been made. Allow follow-through if values are output instead of returned."},{"type":"code","language":"ocr","value":"function pilotValid(pilotCode)\\n  total = 0\\n  for i = 0 to 5\\n    if journeys[i,0] == pilotCode then\\n      temp = float(journeys[i,1])\\n      total = total + temp\\n    endif\\n  next i\\n  if total > 9 then\\n    return \\"warning\\"\\n  else\\n    return \\"valid\\"\\n  endif\\nendfunction"}],"marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Function header pilotValid() with at least one parameter","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks array element [i,0] for each item","marks":1},{"criteria":"Calculates the total hours","marks":1},{"criteria":"Casts journey hours to float/real","marks":1},{"criteria":"Checks whether the total is 9 hours or fewer","marks":1},{"criteria":"Returns warning and valid correctly","marks":1}]},"maps":{"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2023 (2).pdf","question-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/question/page-018.png"]],"markscheme-png":[["data/png/j277/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/markscheme/page-027.png"]],"dev-qa":"e2e/screenshots/yearpapers/paper-2-2023-practice/dev-qa/q-7-f.png"}}]'),nie={"pdf-source":"data/pdf/j277/yearpapers/J27702_Computational_thinking_algorithms_and_programming_Practice_2023 (2).pdf"},oie={paper_id:Kre,qualification:$re,component:eie,title:tie,year:aie,session:rie,total_marks:iie,questions:sie,maps:nie},cie="J277-01-2019-Practice",lie="J277",die="01",pie="Computer Systems",uie=2019,mie="Practice",hie=80,gie=JSON.parse(`[{"question_id":"1(a)(i)","parent_question":1,"topic":"character set definition","marks":1,"command_word":"state","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The ASCII code for the character J is the denary number 74."},{"type":"text","value":"State what is meant by a character set."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for a definition that explains a character set as all the different characters a computer can represent. Do not award 'the set of characters' as this repeats the question.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Definition e.g. all the different characters a computer can represent","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(a)(ii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"ASCII character capacity","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"ASCII has 8 bits per character."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify the maximum number of different characters that ASCII can represent."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Correct answer only: 256.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Correct answer: 256","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(a)(iii)","parent_question":1,"topic":"file size calculation","marks":2,"command_word":"calculate","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A text file uses the ASCII character set. The text file has 2000 characters in it."},{"type":"text","value":"Calculate an estimate of the file size of the text file in Kilobytes. Show your working."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for working, 1 mark for answer. Example working: 2000 * 8 = 16000 bits; 16000 / 8 = 2000 bytes; 2000 / 1000 = 2 Kilobytes. Ignore any overheads e.g. adding 10%.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Working shown (e.g. 2000 * 8 = 16000 bits, then / 8 = 2000 bytes, then / 1000)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correct answer: 2 Kilobytes","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(a)(iv)","parent_question":1,"topic":"alternative character set","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify one other character set."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for naming another character set. Accept: UNICODE.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"UNICODE (or Unicode)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(b)","parent_question":1,"topic":"ASCII binary conversion","marks":1,"command_word":"write","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Write the 8-bit binary number for the ASCII character J in the following boxes:"}],"answer":{"guidance":"Correct answer only (cao): 01001010.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Correct answer: 01001010","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(c)","parent_question":1,"topic":"hexadecimal conversion","marks":2,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the hexadecimal number for the ASCII character K."},{"type":"text","value":"Show your working."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for adding 1 to J (binary 01001011) or showing the conversion from J to hexadecimal and adding 1. 1 mark for the final answer 4B. Allow 1 mark only for converting J to 4A without adding 1.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Adds 1 to J (binary 01001011) / converts J to hex then adds 1","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correct answer: 4B","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"1(d)","parent_question":1,"topic":"binary shift multiplication","marks":2,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A binary shift can be performed on a binary integer."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify which shift will multiply a number by 8."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for left, 1 mark for 3 places. Ignore any reference to arithmetic/logical.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Left (shift direction)","marks":1},{"criteria":"3 places","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"2","parent_question":2,"topic":"digital technology in medicine","marks":8,"command_word":"discuss","content":[{"type":"text","value":"*The use of digital technology in medicine is constantly evolving."},{"type":"text","value":"Discuss the impact of digital technology on medicine including:"},{"type":"text","value":"- diagnosing patients\\n- treating patients\\n- storage of records."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Banded mark scheme. Band 3 (6-8 marks): thorough knowledge and understanding of a wide range of considerations; material is accurate and detailed; applies knowledge directly and consistently to the context; weighs both sides of the discussion; well-developed, logically structured line of reasoning. Band 2 (3-5 marks): reasonable knowledge; material generally accurate but at times underdeveloped; applies knowledge directly but misses one or two opportunities; line of reasoning with some structure. Band 1 (1-2 marks): basic knowledge with limited understanding; unsupported assertions; unstructured communication. 0 marks: no attempt or response not worthy of credit. Indicative content (not prescriptive): Diagnosis - search records faster, identify range of possibilities based on symptoms, identify patterns, more accurate/automated/AI equipment, may miss some symptoms or suggest incorrect results. Treating - AI/automated surgery (can be controlled from another country), access to specialists who are not local, technology may be subject to hacking, software errors could have fatal consequences, may have little human interaction. Storage - centralised storage, all medical staff can access all information about patients from all people involved in care, concerns over privacy and security of data e.g. personal information may be leaked if storage is accessed.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Band 1 (1-2 marks): Basic knowledge with limited understanding; unsupported assertions; unstructured communication","marks":2},{"criteria":"Band 2 (3-5 marks): Reasonable knowledge across a range of considerations; applies knowledge to context with one or two omissions; line of reasoning with some structure","marks":3},{"criteria":"Band 3 (6-8 marks): Thorough, detailed knowledge across diagnosis, treatment and storage; balanced discussion with weighing of both sides; well-developed, logically structured reasoning","marks":3}]}},{"question_id":"3(a)(i)","parent_question":3,"topic":"CPU components identification","marks":4,"command_word":"tick","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The table has five components of a computer, and four statements."},{"type":"text","value":"Tick one or more boxes in each row to identify which component(s) each statement describes."},{"type":"table","headers":["Statement","MAR","MDR","Cache","Program Counter","RAM"],"rows":[["It stores a single address","","","","",""],["It stores frequently used instructions","","","","",""],["It is a register","","","","",""],["It stores all currently running data and instructions","","","","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for correct ticks and gaps on each row. If any extra ticks on a row, 0 marks for that row. Row 1 'It stores a single address': tick MAR only. Row 2 'It stores frequently used instructions': tick Cache only. Row 3 'It is a register': tick MAR, MDR and Program Counter. Row 4 'It stores all currently running data and instructions': tick RAM only.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Row 1 correct: MAR ticked only (for 'It stores a single address')","marks":1},{"criteria":"Row 2 correct: Cache ticked only (for 'It stores frequently used instructions')","marks":1},{"criteria":"Row 3 correct: MAR, MDR and Program Counter all ticked (for 'It is a register')","marks":1},{"criteria":"Row 4 correct: RAM ticked only (for 'It stores all currently running data and instructions')","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"3(a)(ii)","parent_question":3,"topic":"register name and purpose","marks":2,"command_word":"identify and describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify the name of one register not given 