are often built into a ____ machine. Two examples of embedded systems are a ____ and automated ____ in a car."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for each completed term. Gap 1: functions. Gap 2: larger. Gap 3: washing machine. Gap 4: lights.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Gap 1: functions","marks":1},{"criteria":"Gap 2: larger","marks":1},{"criteria":"Gap 3: washing machine","marks":1},{"criteria":"Gap 4: lights","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(a)","parent_question":5,"topic":"image storage true or false","marks":2,"command_word":"tick","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Layla is an artist. She draws images by hand. The image is then scanned and stored on a computer."},{"type":"text","value":"The table has four statements about the storage of images on a computer."},{"type":"text","value":"Tick one box in each row to identify if the statement is true or false."},{"type":"table","headers":["Statement","True","False"],"rows":[["Each colour has a unique binary code","",""],["Metadata stores the colour of each pixel in the image","",""],["A bitmap is made of pixels","",""],["The higher the colour depth, the smaller the number of different colours that can be displayed","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for 2 correct ticks; 2 marks for all 4 correct ticks. Two ticks in one row is incorrect. Correct answers: Each colour has a unique binary code = True; Metadata stores the colour of each pixel in the image = False; A bitmap is made of pixels = True; The higher the colour depth, the smaller the number of different colours that can be displayed = False.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"At least 2 of the 4 rows ticked correctly (True for 'unique binary code' and 'bitmap is made of pixels'; False for 'metadata stores the colour of each pixel' and 'higher colour depth, smaller number of colours')","marks":1},{"criteria":"All 4 rows ticked correctly","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(b)(i)","parent_question":5,"topic":"storage capacity calculation","marks":2,"command_word":"calculate","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Layla stores her images on a secondary storage device."},{"type":"text","value":"Each image has a fixed size of 1 MB. The storage device has a capacity of 3 GB."},{"type":"text","value":"Calculate how many images can be saved on the storage device. Show your working."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for working, 1 mark for answer. Working: 1000 * 3 (there are 1000 MB in 1 GB, so 3 GB = 3000 MB). Answer: 3000 images.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Working shown (e.g. 1000 * 3, or 3 GB = 3000 MB)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Correct answer: 3000 images","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(b)(ii)","parent_question":5,"topic":"storage device selection","marks":3,"command_word":"identify and justify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Layla uses the images to make videos. These videos are stored on her computer's internal storage device."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify the most appropriate type of storage device for Layla to use in her computer. Justify your choice."},{"type":"text","value":"Type of storage device: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"Justification: ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for a suitable type: solid state or magnetic. Then 1 mark per bullet of justification to max 2, with points matching the chosen type. Solid state justifications: large enough capacity; can move computer without damaging storage; faster access speeds. Magnetic justifications: largest capacity; computer is not moved so moving parts do not matter; more reliable long-term.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Suitable type identified: solid state or magnetic","marks":1},{"criteria":"Justification point 1 matching the chosen type (e.g. solid state: faster access / not damaged when moved; magnetic: largest capacity / reliable long-term)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Justification point 2 matching the chosen type","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(b)(iii)","parent_question":5,"topic":"sound storage true or false","marks":3,"command_word":"tick","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The videos include sound. The table has statements about the storage of sound in a computer."},{"type":"text","value":"Tick one box in each row to identify if the statement is true or false."},{"type":"table","headers":["Statement","True","False"],"rows":[["The sample rate is the number of times the amplitude is recorded per second","",""],["The smaller the bit depth the smaller the range of sounds recorded","",""],["The larger the sample rate the larger the bit depth","",""],["The frequency and pitch of the sound wave are measured","",""],["Sound is stored using pixels","",""]]}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for 2 correct ticks; 2 marks for 3 or 4 correct ticks; 3 marks for all 5 correct. Two ticks in one row is incorrect. Correct answers: sample rate is number of times amplitude is recorded per second = True; smaller the bit depth, smaller the range of sounds recorded = True; larger sample rate means larger bit depth = False; frequency and pitch of the sound wave are measured = False; sound is stored using pixels = False.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"At least 2 rows ticked correctly","marks":1},{"criteria":"At least 3 or 4 rows ticked correctly","marks":1},{"criteria":"All 5 rows ticked correctly (True, True, False, False, False in order)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(c)(i)","parent_question":5,"topic":"compression reasons","marks":2,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Layla uploads her images and videos to a website."},{"type":"text","value":"Explain why Layla compresses the images and videos before uploading them."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark per bullet to max 2. Points: reduces the file size; takes up less space on the server; faster upload to server; faster download for users.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Reduces file size / takes up less space on the server","marks":1},{"criteria":"Faster upload to server / faster download for users","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(c)(ii)","parent_question":5,"topic":"compression method choice","marks":3,"command_word":"identify and justify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Layla wants to reduce the file size of the images and videos by the largest amount possible."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify the method of compression that would be most appropriate. Justify your choice."},{"type":"text","value":"Compression method: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"Justification: ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for lossy. 1 mark per bullet of justification to max 2. Justifications: lossy will most likely reduce the file size by a larger amount than lossless; lossy will remove data that is not noticeable, so changes allow further reduction without the user noticing. Award follow-through marks for justifying lossless appropriately to max 2.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Compression method: lossy","marks":1},{"criteria":"Justification point 1 (e.g. lossy reduces file size by a larger amount than lossless)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Justification point 2 (e.g. lossy removes data that is not noticeable / user will not notice the changes)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(d)","parent_question":5,"topic":"copyright legislation","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Layla wants to protect her images so they cannot be copied by other people."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify which legislation can help protect Layla's images."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for naming the relevant legislation: Copyright, Designs and Patents Act.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Copyright, Designs and Patents Act","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(a)","parent_question":6,"topic":"network type identification","marks":1,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Amir has a home network that includes two laptop computers, four mobile phones, and two televisions."},{"type":"text","value":"Identify the type of network Amir has at home."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for LAN or Local Area Network.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"LAN / Local Area Network","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(b)(i)","parent_question":6,"topic":"switch vs router","marks":6,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The network uses a star topology with a central switch. The switch has an integrated wireless access point (WAP)."},{"type":"text","value":"Describe the similarities and differences between a switch and a router."},{"type":"text","value":"Similarities: ____"},{"type":"text","value":"Differences: ____"}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark per bullet. Maximum 4 marks for similarities and maximum 4 marks for differences, overall total 6. Similarities: they both connect devices; they receive data from the devices; they determine the correct destination for the data; they transmit the data to its destination. Differences: a switch uses MAC addresses; a router uses IPs; a switch connects nodes/computers; a router connects networks/Internet; a router stores the addresses of devices attached; a switch records the addresses as they are accessed (a switch has to look for the correct address before sending).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Similarity: both connect devices / receive data from devices","marks":1},{"criteria":"Similarity: determine the correct destination / transmit data to its destination","marks":1},{"criteria":"Difference: a switch uses MAC addresses, a router uses IP addresses","marks":1},{"criteria":"Difference: a switch connects nodes/computers within a network; a router connects networks / connects to the Internet","marks":1},{"criteria":"Difference: a router stores the addresses of devices attached to it","marks":1},{"criteria":"Difference: a switch records addresses as they are accessed / has to look up the correct address before sending","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6(b)(ii)","parent_question":6,"topic":"star topology diagram","marks":3,"command_word":"draw","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Draw the star topology for Amir's home network. Clearly label each devi