":[{"criteria":"A computer system that is built into another device","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"3(c)","parent_question":3,"topic":"embedded system examples","marks":3,"command_word":"identify","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify three devices, other than a Sat Nav, which contain embedded systems."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for each correct example identified, to a maximum of 3 marks. Accept: dishwasher, MP3 player, washing machine, mobile phone, manufacturing equipment. There are many other examples of devices with embedded systems which may be acceptable.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"First valid device with an embedded system (e.g. dishwasher, MP3 player, washing machine, mobile phone, manufacturing equipment)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Second valid device with an embedded system (different from the first)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Third valid device with an embedded system (different from the first two)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"4(a)","parent_question":4,"topic":"sound recording process","marks":2,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A computer records an audio file of someone playing a guitar."},{"type":"text","value":"Describe what happens when the computer converts the music into a file."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for each bullet, to a maximum of 2 marks. Accept: the height of the wave is measured / sampled (at regular / set intervals); turned into / stored as binary.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"The height of the (sound) wave is measured / sampled (at regular/set intervals)","marks":1},{"criteria":"(The samples are) turned into / stored as binary","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"4(b)","parent_question":4,"topic":"sample rate effects","marks":2,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The sample rate is increased on the computer when recording the guitar."},{"type":"text","value":"Give two effects this will have on the recording."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for each bullet, to a maximum of 2 marks. Accept: the quality will improve; the file size will increase.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"The (sound) quality will improve","marks":1},{"criteria":"The file size will increase","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(a)","parent_question":5,"topic":"binary to denary conversion","marks":1,"command_word":"convert","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Convert the binary number 11001011 into denary."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Correct answer only: 203.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Correct answer: 203","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(b)","parent_question":5,"topic":"binary shift right","marks":1,"command_word":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Complete a 2-place shift to the right on the binary number 11001011."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Correct answer only: 00110010.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Correct answer: 00110010","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"5(c)","parent_question":5,"topic":"binary shift effect","marks":2,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Explain the effect of performing a 2-place shift to the right on the binary number 11001011."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for each correct point, to a maximum of 2 marks. Accept: divides the number by 4; loses precision (the two bits shifted off the end are lost).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Divides the number by 4","marks":1},{"criteria":"Loses precision (bits shifted off the end are lost)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"6","parent_question":6,"topic":"ASCII representation","marks":2,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The table gives the ASCII code for the characters."},{"type":"table","headers":["Character","ASCII code"],"rows":[["L","76"],["M","77"],["N","78"],["O","79"],["P","80"]]},{"type":"text","value":"Explain how the word MOP will be represented in ASCII."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark per bullet, to a maximum of 2 marks. Accept: each character from MOP has its ASCII code stored in the order written - 77 79 80 (MOP); ASCII code converted to 8-bit binary number.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Each character from MOP has its ASCII code stored in the order written (e.g. 77, 79, 80)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Each ASCII code is converted to (and stored as) an 8-bit binary number","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(a)","parent_question":7,"topic":"network protocol definition","marks":1,"command_word":"define","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The owners of a large bakery have a Local Area Network (LAN) with a star topology. They order their supplies over the Internet. When data is transmitted from the bakery to the supplier, network protocols are used."},{"type":"text","value":"Define what is meant by a 'network protocol'."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark only for a correct definition: a set of rules for communication.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"A set of rules for communication (between devices on a network)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(b)(i)","parent_question":7,"topic":"protocol layer definition","marks":1,"command_word":"define","content":[{"type":"text","value":"TCP/IP is a set of protocols based on layers."},{"type":"text","value":"With regards to network protocols, define what is meant by a 'layer'."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for a correct definition. Accept: a division of network functionality. Candidate's responses may differ from the given answer but must represent conceptually the same thing - e.g. 'a layer is where jobs / processes are split up' would receive the mark.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"A division of network functionality (e.g. where jobs / processes are split up)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(b)(ii)","parent_question":7,"topic":"protocol layer advantage","marks":2,"command_word":"describe","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Describe one advantage of using layers to construct network protocols."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for the correct identification and 1 mark for a valid description, to a maximum of 2 marks. Accept: it is self-contained (1) so it allows different developers to concentrate on one aspect of the network (1); a layer can be taken out and edited without affecting other layers (1) so it promotes interoperability between vendors and systems (1).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Identifies a valid advantage (e.g. layers are self-contained / a layer can be edited without affecting other layers)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Provides a valid description / consequence (e.g. allows developers to concentrate on one aspect, promotes interoperability between vendors and systems)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"7(c)","parent_question":7,"topic":"star topology reasons","marks":2,"command_word":"give","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Give two reasons why the bakery may use a star network topology for their LAN."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for each correct reason, to a maximum of 2 marks. Accept: it is easy to add a new node or device; fewer data collisions can occur; if a node or device fails it does not affect the rest of the network; a signal does not need to be transmitted to all computers in the network. Any valid comparisons to other topologies can be awarded marks.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"First valid reason (e.g. easy to add a new node/device, fewer data collisions, node failure does not affect the rest of the network, signal not transmitted to all computers)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Second valid reason (different from the first)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(a)","parent_question":8,"topic":"network security methods","marks":6,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A hospital stores patients' details on its computer network. The hospital is concerned about the security of its patients' details."},{"type":"text","value":"Staff already use strong passwords to protect systems. Explain, with reference to system security, three other ways that the hospital could protect the network system."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark to be awarded for each correct type to a maximum of 3 marks (AO2 1a). 1 mark to be awarded for each correct explanation to a maximum of 3 marks (AO2 1b). Accept: Firewall - prevents unauthorised access; Anti-malware - removes viruses / spyware from infecting the system; Encryption - any intercepted data is rendered useless; User access levels - users have restricted access; Network policies - rules that define acceptable use.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"First security method identified (e.g. firewall, anti-malware, encryption, user access levels, network policies)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Explanation of the first method (e.g. firewall prevents unauthorised access)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Second security method identified (different from the first)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Explanation of the second method","marks":1},{"criteria":"Third security method identified (different from the first two)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Explanation of the third method","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"8(b)","parent_question":8,"topic":"network security errors","marks":6,"command_word":"identify and outline","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Identify three errors that the hospital staff could make that may endanger the security of the network. Outline a procedure that could be put in place to prevent each error."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark to be awarded for each correct identification of an error to a maximum of 3 marks (AO2 1a). 1 mark to be awarded for each correct outlining of a procedure to a maximum of 3 marks (AO2 1b). Allow any reasonable combination of error and procedure to mitigate the risk. Accept: brings in files via any medium / not allowing or stopping external devices being used on the network; downloading infected files from the internet / blocking or restricting access to insecure websites; allowing physical access to the network / locking of doors, key cards or any physical security procedure; sending or sharing sensitive data with third parties / blocking or restricting access to USB ports, email, internet or printing.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"First error identified (e.g. bringing in files via external media, downloading infected files, allowing physical access, sharing sensitive data with third parties)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Procedure that mitigates the first error (e.g. block external devices, restrict insecure websites, lock doors / use key cards, restrict USB / email / printing)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Second error identified (different from the first)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Procedure that mitigates the second error","marks":1},{"criteria":"Third error identified (different from the first two)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Procedure that mitigates the third error","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9(a)","parent_question":9,"topic":"disk fragmentation cause","marks":4,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A restaurant has a computer-based ordering system which is running slowly. A technician has said that the hard disc drive is fragmented. The technician has suggested using utility software to defragment the drive."},{"type":"text","value":"Explain how the restaurant's hard disc could have become fragmented."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Up to a maximum of 4 marks. A maximum of three marks if there is no contextualisation. Allow a mark if candidates state that fragmentation increases access time. Accept: orders have been saved onto the system as they order food and then deleted once processed (1); once other orders have been made, new files are created (1) which may be bigger than the spaces left by the deleted files (1); the order files are split up (1).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Order files are saved to the disc as customers order food and deleted once processed","marks":1},{"criteria":"As more orders are made, new files are created (and saved into the available spaces)","marks":1},{"criteria":"New files may be bigger than the spaces left by the deleted files","marks":1},{"criteria":"The (order) files are split up / stored in non-contiguous blocks across the disc","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"9(b)","parent_question":9,"topic":"defragmentation software","marks":3,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Explain how defragmentation software could overcome the issue of the slow computer system."}],"answer":{"guidance":"Up to a maximum of 3 marks. Accept: files on the hard disk drive are moved (1); empty spaces collected together (1); files are moved to be stored together (1); fewer disc accesses are needed (1).","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Files on the hard disk drive are moved (rearranged)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Empty spaces are collected together / files belonging to the same file are stored together (contiguously)","marks":1},{"criteria":"Fewer disc accesses are needed (so the system runs faster)","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(a)","parent_question":10,"topic":"WAN definition","marks":1,"command_word":"define","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A law company currently use a Local Area Network (LAN) linked to a Wide Area Network (WAN)."},{"type":"text","value":"They want to upgrade their system to utilise cloud storage."},{"type":"text","value":"Define what is meant by a Wide Area Network."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark only for a correct definition. Accept: the computers are geographically remote / distanced / more than a mile apart; communication medium is not owned by the law firm (e.g. the company doesn't own the infrastructure). Do not accept 'network over a wide area' or similar arrangement of wording.","marks_breakdown":[{"criteria":"Computers are geographically remote/distanced (more than a mile apart) and/or the communication medium/infrastructure is not owned by the organisation","marks":1}]}},{"question_id":"10(b)","parent_question":10,"topic":"cloud storage advantages","marks":4,"command_word":"explain","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Explain two advantages to the law company of storing their data in the Cloud."}],"answer":{"guidance":"1 mark for each correct advantage,